de-Circus.pdf.pdf'),(3127,379,'_wp_attachment_metadata','a:2:{s:5:\"sizes\";a:4:{s:4:\"full\";a:5:{s:4:\"file\";s:62:\"JUGGLING-BALLS-Activity-Info-Sheet-Homemade-Circus.pdf-pdf.jpg\";s:5:\"width\";i:1059;s:6:\"height\";i:1497;s:9:\"mime-type\";s:10:\"image/jpeg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:198642;}s:6:\"medium\";a:5:{s:4:\"file\";s:70:\"JUGGLING-BALLS-Activity-Info-Sheet-Homemade-Circus.pdf-pdf-212x300.jpg\";s:5:\"width\";i:212;s:6:\"height\";i:300;s:9:\"mime-type\";s:10:\"image/jpeg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:15785;}s:5:\"large\";a:5:{s:4:\"file\";s:71:\"JUGGLING-BALLS-Activity-Info-Sheet-Homemade-Circus.pdf-pdf-724x1024.jpg\";s:5:\"width\";i:724;s:6:\"height\";i:1024;s:9:\"mime-type\";s:10:\"image/jpeg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:103175;}s:9:\"thumbnail\";a:5:{s:4:\"file\";s:70:\"JUGGLING-BALLS-Activity-Info-Sheet-Homemade-Circus.pdf-pdf-106x150.jpg\";s:5:\"width\";i:106;s:6:\"height\";i:150;s:9:\"mime-type\";s:10:\"image/jpeg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:6962;}}s:8:\"filesize\";i:2246519;}'),(3128,381,'footnotes',''),(3130,383,'footnotes',''),(3133,386,'footnotes',''),(3139,44,'faq_3_question','How long will a session take to run?'),(3140,44,'_faq_3_question','field_658489486da97'),(3141,44,'faq_3_answer','<p class=\"Body\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-family: \'Century Gothic\',sans-serif;\">If you want to run a full session, we recommend 45-60 minutes of uninterrupted circus activity. Ideally, you should allow time before the session whilst people are entering the room and add some time at the end of the session for a gentle warm-down and socialising afterwards. We will guide you through running your first circus session in the \'Planning Your Workshop\' section of the toolkit.<u></u></span></p>'),(3142,44,'_faq_3_answer','field_658489586da98'),(3143,44,'faq_4_question','Who can take part?'),(3144,44,'_faq_4_question','field_658489486da97'),(3145,44,'faq_4_answer','We have done extensive testing and research to choose the most accessible and adaptable activities for the Digital Toolkit. Every activity can be changed to suit someone\'s needs, and we show you how to do this in our video tutorials. We wanted to ensure no one was \'counted out\' when it came to who can take part. As a result, absolutely anyone can take part in these activities, including those with dementia, those living with cognitive/physical impairments, and activities can also be taken to those who are not able to move from their beds. We have seen some of the best results and changes in people who care home staff initially thought might not be able to take part.'),(3146,44,'_faq_4_answer','field_658489586da98'),(3147,44,'faq_5_question','Where can I buy circus equipment?'),(3148,44,'_faq_5_question','field_658489486da97'),(3149,44,'faq_5_answer','<p class=\"Body\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-family: \'Century Gothic\',sans-serif;\">We will provide you with links to the websites of circus equipment providers in the UK where you can purchase equipment for all of the activities that we teach you in our videos. </span></p>'),(3150,44,'_faq_5_answer','field_658489586da98'),(3323,408,'_edit_lock','1787229312:3'),(3326,408,'_edit_last','3'),(3327,408,'image','431'),(3328,408,'_image','field_64cd0e8559eb8'),(3329,408,'side_info','1'),(3330,408,'_side_info','field_649f23a3df204'),(3335,408,'download','1'),(3336,408,'_download','field_64c2860925422'),(3337,408,'links_0_link_title','Buy Blocks'),(3338,408,'_links_0_link_title','field_64c2875e34e17'),(3339,408,'links_0_link_url','https://www.ebay.co.uk/itm/334924037856'),(3340,408,'_links_0_link_url','field_64c2875e34e18'),(3345,408,'links','1'),(3346,408,'_links','field_64c2875e34e16'),(3347,408,'_mepr_unauthorized_message_type','default'),(3348,408,'_mepr_unauthorized_message',''),(3349,408,'_mepr_unauth_login','default'),(3350,408,'_mepr_unauth_excerpt_type','default'),(3351,408,'_mepr_unauth_excerpt_size','100'),(3352,410,'_wp_attached_file','2024/03/BLOCKS-Activity-Info-Sheet-Homemade-Circus.pdf'),(3353,410,'_wp_attachment_meta