e focus and reaction times with juggling balls. Learn how to introduce them in group exercises and explore advanced techniques in this helpful video tutorial.'),(4092,18,'_yoast_wpseo_linkdex','81'),(4093,18,'_yoast_wpseo_content_score','90'),(4094,18,'_yoast_wpseo_estimated-reading-time-minutes','2'),(4095,18,'_yoast_wpseo_wordproof_timestamp',''),(4138,24,'_yoast_wpseo_focuskw','Homemade Circus'),(4139,24,'_yoast_wpseo_linkdex','7'),(4140,24,'_yoast_wpseo_estimated-reading-time-minutes','0'),(4141,24,'_yoast_wpseo_wordproof_timestamp',''),(4227,24,'_yoast_wpseo_metadesc','Learn to lead inspiring circus sessions in your care home with Homemade Circus. Instructional videos, activity worksheets, and expert guidance, you\'ll have the skills and confidence to lead inspiring circus activities for your residents.'),(4231,484,'_wp_attached_file','2024/04/20230313-7R404981-Edit-1-e1714065044395.jpg'),(4232,484,'_wp_attachment_metadata','a:6:{s:5:\"width\";i:1500;s:6:\"height\";i:470;s:4:\"file\";s:51:\"2024/04/20230313-7R404981-Edit-1-e1714065044395.jpg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:744084;s:5:\"sizes\";a:4:{s:6:\"medium\";a:5:{s:4:\"file\";s:50:\"20230313-7R404981-Edit-1-e1714065044395-300x94.jpg\";s:5:\"width\";i:300;s:6:\"height\";i:94;s:9:\"mime-type\";s:10:\"image/jpeg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:19327;}s:5:\"large\";a:5:{s:4:\"file\";s:52:\"20230313-7R404981-Edit-1-e1714065044395-1024x321.jpg\";s:5:\"width\";i:1024;s:6:\"height\";i:321;s:9:\"mime-type\";s:10:\"image/jpeg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:77082;}s:9:\"thumbnail\";a:5:{s:4:\"file\";s:51:\"20230313-7R404981-Edit-1-e1714065044395-150x150.jpg\";s:5:\"width\";i:150;s:6:\"height\";i:150;s:9:\"mime-type\";s:10:\"image/jpeg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:17586;}s:12:\"medium_large\";a:5:{s:4:\"file\";s:51:\"20230313-7R404981-Edit-1-e1714065044395-768x241.jpg\";s:5:\"width\";i:768;s:6:\"height\";i:241;s:9:\"mime-type\";s:10:\"image/jpeg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:52797;}}s:10:\"image_meta\";a:12:{s:8:\"aperture\";s:3:\"2.8\";s:6:\"credit\";s:19:\"Christopher Andreou\";s:6:\"camera\";s:9:\"ILCE-7RM4\";s:7:\"caption\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"created_timestamp\";s:10:\"1678716712\";s:9:\"copyright\";s:31:\"Christopher Andreou Photography\";s:12:\"focal_length\";s:2:\"24\";s:3:\"iso\";s:3:\"250\";s:13:\"shutter_speed\";s:17:\"0.016666666666667\";s:5:\"title\";s:0:\"\";s:11:\"orientation\";s:1:\"1\";s:8:\"keywords\";a:0:{}}}'),(4233,484,'_wp_attachment_backup_sizes','a:10:{s:9:\"full-orig\";a:3:{s:5:\"width\";i:1500;s:6:\"height\";i:1000;s:4:\"file\";s:28:\"20230313-7R404981-Edit-1.jpg\";}s:14:\"thumbnail-orig\";a:5:{s:4:\"file\";s:36:\"20230313-7R404981-Edit-1-150x150.jpg\";s:5:\"width\";i:150;s:6:\"height\";i:150;s:9:\"mime-type\";s:10:\"image/jpeg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:18154;}s:11:\"medium-orig\";a:5:{s:4:\"file\";s:36:\"20230313-7R404981-Edit-1-300x200.jpg\";s:5:\"width\";i:300;s:6:\"height\";i:200;s:9:\"mime-type\";s:10:\"image/jpeg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:28303;}s:17:\"medium_large-orig\";a:5:{s:4:\"file\";s:36:\"20230313-7R404981-Edit-1-768x512.jpg\";s:5:\"width\";i:768;s:6:\"height\";i:512;s:9:\"mime-type\";s:10:\"image/jpeg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:93794;}s:10:\"large-orig\";a:5:{s:4:\"file\";s:37:\"20230313-7R404981-Edit-1-1024x683.jpg\";s:5:\"width\";i:1024;s:6:\"height\";i:683;s:9:\"mime-type\";s:10:\"image/jpeg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:144379;}s:18:\"full-1714065044395\";a:3:{s:5:\"width\";i:1500;s:6:\"height\";i:577;s:4:\"file\";s:43:\"20230313-7R404981-Edit-1-e1714064953940.jpg\";}s:23:\"thumbnail-1714065044395\";a:5:{s:4:\"file\";s:51:\"20230313-7R404981-Edit-1-e1714064953940-150x150.jpg\";s:5:\"width\";i:150;s:6:\"height\";i:150;s:9:\"mime-type\";s:10:\"image/jpeg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:17677;}s:20:\"medium-1714065044395\";a:5:{s:4:\"file\";s:51:\"20230313-7R404981-Edit-1-e1714064953940-300x115.jpg\";s:5:\"width\";i:300;s:6:\"height\";i:115;s:9:\"mime-type\";s:10:\"image/jpeg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:21427;}s:26:\"medium_large-1714065044395\";a:5:{s:4:\"file\";s:51:\"20230313-7R404981-Edit-1-e1714064953940-768x295.jpg\";s:5:\"width\";i:768;s:6:\"height\";i:295;s:9:\"mime-type\";s:10:\"image/jpeg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:60163;}s:19:\"large-1714065044395\";a:5:{s:4:\"file\";s:52:\"20230313-7R404981-Edit-1-e1714064953940-1024x394.jpg\";s:5:\"width\";i:1024;s:6:\"height\";i:394;s:9:\"mime-type\";s:10:\"image/jpeg\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:89242;}}'),(4260,44,'_yoast_wpseo_focuskw','FAQs'),(4261,44,'_yoast_wpseo_metadesc','Get answers to FAQs about Homemade Circus Digital Toolkit. Learn about leading circus activities, fitting them into your schedule, buying equipment, and the benefits for care homes.'),(4262,44,'_yoast_wpseo_linkdex','44'),(4263,44,'_yoast_wpseo_content_score','90'),(4264,44,'_yoast_wpseo_estimated-reading-time-minutes','1'),(4265,44,'_yoast_wpseo_wordproof_timestamp',''),(4293,488,'faq_0_question','What is Homemade Circus?'),(4294,488,'_faq_0_question','field_658489486da97'),(4295,488,'faq_0_answer','<p class=\"Body\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-family: \'Century Gothic\',sans-serif;\">Homemade Circus is a two-year project created by Upswing - delivering Circus activities in care homes across London and the Southeast. Upswing is working with care home staff and activity coordinators from Anchor, Excelcare, and Agin Care. Funded by City Bridge Trust and The Rayne Foundation, the project aims to deliver practical Circus activities for and with people living in care homes, and to train and upskill care home staff so that they can deliver circus sessions for the people living in their homes. </span></p>\r\n<p class=\"Body\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-family: \'Century Gothic\',sans-serif;\">Upswing’s Digital Toolkit is a central part of Homemade Circus and aims to be an online resource for care home staff to find accessible resources on leading Circus activities in their own care home setting. You can learn more about our journey with circus and older people <a href=\"https://upswing.org.uk/learning/circus-and-older-people/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">here</a>.</span></p>'),(4296,488,'_faq_0_answer','field_658489586da98'),(4297,488,'faq_1_question','How can I lead circus activities without any experience?'),(4298,488,'_faq_1_question','field_658489486da97'),(4299,488,'faq_1_answer','<p class=\"Body\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-family: \'Century Gothic\',sans-serif;\">Upswing’s Toolkit will show you step-by-step how you to use Circus equipment (such as juggling balls, coloured scarves and hats) to work with participants to improve their dexterity, mobility, concentration and to lift the mood of your home. The toolkit is made with complete beginners in mind! We will guide you from start to finish.</span></p>'),(4300,488,'_faq_1_answer','field_658489586da98'),(4301,488,'faq_2_question','How can we fit these into a busy schedule?'),(4302,488,'_faq_2_question','field_658489486da97'),(4303,488,'faq_2_answer','<p class=\"Body\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-family: \'Century Gothic\',sans-serif;\">Some of these activities can be delivered on a one-to-one basis in 5 -10mins to encourage interaction between staff and residents and can even be used in people\'s rooms for those that cannot travel down to a communal space. Even just a short session can bring benefits to your staff and the people who live in your home. You could consider scheduling a regular weekly session at the same time each week so that people know when the session is happening.</span></p>'),(4304,488,'_faq_2_answer','field_658489586da98'),(4305,488,'faq','6'),(4306,488,'_faq','field_658489286da96'),(4307,488,'faq_3_question','How long will a session take to run?'),(4308,488,'_faq_3_question','field_658489486da97'),(4309,488,'faq_3_answer','<p class=\"Body\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-family: \'Century Gothic\',sans-serif;\">We suggest a session of 45-60 minutes of uninterrupted circus activity. Ideally, you should allow time before the session whilst people are entering the room and add some time at the end of the session for a gentle warm-down and socialising afterwards.<u></u></span></p>'),(4310,488,'_faq_3_answer','field_658489586da98'),(4311,488,'faq_4_question','Where can I buy circus equipment?'),(4312,488,'_faq_4_question','field_658489486da97'),(4313,488,'faq_4_answer','<p class=\"Body\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-family: \'Century Gothic\',sans-serif;\">We will provide you with links to the websites of circus equipment providers in the UK where you can purchase juggling balls, coloured scarves and flower sticks. You can also use other equipment available from online providers – we also use beach balls, parachutes, gymnastic ribbons and peacock feathers in our sessions. </span></p>'),(4314,488,'_faq_4_answer','field_658489586da98'),(4315,488,'faq_5_question','Why should I introduce circus activities to my care home? '),(4316,488,'_faq_5_question','field_658489486da97'),(4317,488,'faq_5_answer','<ul>\r\n 	<li>Taking part in Circus activities can improve the quality of life for people who live in care homes who may have dementia or a range of physical disabilities</li>\r\n 	<li>Circus activities are beneficial for increasing physical movement, collaboration and alertness, verbal and non-verbal communication, and improving quality of life</li>\r\n 	<li>Circus activities can decrease anxiety and agitation uplifting the mood and feel of the individual or group</li>\r\n 	<li>Circus activities can strengthen social interaction between care staff and the people they are caring for, and bring people who live in care homes together in a shared experience. This is particularly important in terms of redressing the isolation caused by the Covid-19 pandemic</li>\r\n 	<li>Circus equipment is intriguing - the equipment is very tactile and sensory, it is easy to pick up, hold, squeeze and interact with – the bright colours and unusual look make you want to pick up and explore the equipment</li>\r\n 	<li>Circus activities can be scaled up or scaled down to meet the needs of individual participants who may have different levels of mobility. We will show you how to use the different types of equipment and how you can adapt the session to make it easier or more challenging based on the needs of the participants</li>\r\n</ul>'),(4318,488,'_faq_5_answer','field_658489586da98'),(4346,490,'faq_0_question','What is Homemade Circus?'),(4347,490,'_faq_0_question','field_658489486da97'),(4348,490,'faq_0_answer','<p class=\"Body\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-family: \'Century Gothic\',sans-serif;\">Homemade Circus is a two-year project created by Upswing - delivering Circus activities in care homes across London and the Southeast. Upswing is working with care home staff and activity coordinators from Anchor, Excelcare, and Agin Care. Funded by City Bridge Trust and The Rayne Foundation, the project aims to deliver practical Circus activities for and with people living in care homes, and to train and upskill care home staff so that they can deliver circus sessions for the people living in their homes. </span></p>\r\n<p class=\"Body\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-family: \'Century Gothic\',sans-serif;\">Upswing’s Digital Toolkit is a central part of Homemade Circus and aims to be an online resource for care home staff to find accessible resources on leading Circus activities in their own care home setting. You can learn more about our journey with circus and older people <a href=\"https://upswing.org.uk/learning/circus-and-older-people/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">here</a>.</span></p>'),(4349,490,'_faq_0_answer','field_658489586da98'),(4350,490,'faq_1_question','How can I lead circus activities without any experience?'),(4351,490,'_faq_1_question','field_658489486da97'),(4352,490,'faq_1_answer','<p class=\"Body\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-family: \'Century Gothic\',sans-serif;\">Upswing’s Toolkit will show you step-by-step how you to use Circus equipment (such as juggling balls, coloured scarves and hats) to work with participants to improve their dexterity, mobility, concentration and to lift the mood of your home. The toolkit is made with complete beginners in mind! We will guide you from start to finish.</span></p>'),(4353,490,'_faq_1_answer','field_658489586da98'),(4354,490,'faq_2_question','How can we fit these into a busy schedule?'),(4355,490,'_faq_2_question','field_658489486da97'),(4356,490,'faq_2_answer','<p class=\"Body\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-family: \'Century Gothic\',sans-serif;\">Some of these activities can be delivered on a one-to-one basis in 5 -10mins to encourage interaction between staff and residents and can even be used in people\'s rooms for those that cannot travel down to a communal space. Even just a short session can bring benefits to your staff and the people who live in your home. You could consider scheduling a regular weekly session at the same time each week so that people know when the session is happening.</span></p>'),(4357,490,'_faq_2_answer','field_658489586da98'),(4358,490,'faq','6'),(4359,490,'_faq','field_658489286da96'),(4360,490,'faq_3_question','How long will a session take to run?'),(4361,490,'_faq_3_question','field_658489486da97'),(4362,490,'faq_3_answer','<p class=\"Body\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-family: \'Century Gothic\',sans-serif;\">We suggest a session of 45-60 minutes of uninterrupted circus activity. Ideally, you should allow time before the session whilst people are entering the room and add some time at the end of the session for a gentle warm-down and socialising afterwards.<u></u></span></p>'),(4363,490,'_faq_3_answer','field_658489586da98'),(4364,490,'faq_4_question','Where can I buy circus equipment?'),(4365,490,'_faq_4_question','field_658489486da97'),(4366,490,'faq_4_answer','<p class=\"Body\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-family: \'Century Gothic\',sans-serif;\">We will provide you with links to the websites of circus equipment providers in the UK where you can purchase juggling balls, coloured scarves and flower sticks. You can also use other equipment available from online providers – we also use beach balls, parachutes, gymnastic ribbons and peacock feathers in our sessions. </span></p>'),(4367,490,'_faq_4_answer','field_658489586da98'),(4368,490,'faq_5_question','Why should I introduce circus activities to my care home? '),(4369,490,'_faq_5_question','field_658489486da97'),(4370,490,'faq_5_answer','<ul>\r\n 	<li>Taking part in Circus activities can improve the quality of life for people who live in care homes who may have dementia or a range of physical disabilities</li>\r\n 	<li>Circus activities are beneficial for increasing physical movement, collaboration and alertness, verbal and non-verbal communication, and improving quality of life</li>\r\n 	<li>Circus activities can decrease anxiety and agitation uplifting the mood and feel of the individual or group</li>\r\n 	<li>Circus activities can strengthen social interaction between care staff and the people they are caring for, and bring people who live in care homes together in a shared experience. This is particularly important in terms of redressing the isolation caused by the Covid-19 pandemic</li>\r\n 	<li>Circus equipment is intriguing - the equipment is very tactile and sensory, it is easy to pick up, hold, squeeze and interact with – the bright colours and unusual look make you want to pick up and explore the equipment</li>\r\n 	<li>Circus activities can be scaled up or scaled down to meet the needs of individual participants who may have different levels of mobility. We will show you how to use the different types of equipment and how you can adapt the session to make it easier or more challenging based on the needs of the participants</li>\r\n</ul>'),(4371,490,'_faq_5_answer','field_658489586da98'),(4372,491,'faq_0_question','What is Homemade Circus?'),(4373,491,'_faq_0_question','field_658489486da97'),(4374,491,'faq_0_answer','<p class=\"Body\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-family: \'Century Gothic\',sans-serif;\">Homemade Circus is a two-year project created by Upswing - delivering Circus activities in care homes across London and the Southeast. Upswing is working with care home staff and activity coordinators from Anchor, Excelcare, and BUPA. Funded by City Bridge Trust and The Rayne Foundation, the project aims to deliver practical Circus activities for and with people living in care homes, and to train and upskill care home staff so that they can deliver circus sessions for the people living in their homes. </span></p>\r\n<p class=\"Body\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-family: \'Century Gothic\',sans-serif;\">Upswing’s Digital Toolkit is a central part of Homemade Circus and aims to be an online resource for care home staff to find accessible resources on leading Circus activities in their own care home setting. You can learn more about our journey with circus and older people <a href=\"https://upswing.org.uk/learning/circus-and-older-people/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">here</a>.</span></p>'),(4375,491,'_faq_0_answer','field_658489586da98'),(4376,491,'faq_1_question','How can I lead circus activities without any experience?'),(4377,491,'_faq_1_question','field_658489486da97'),(4378,491,'faq_1_answer','<p class=\"Body\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-family: \'Century Gothic\',sans-serif;\">Upswing’s Toolkit will show you step-by-step how you to use Circus equipment (such as juggling balls, coloured scarves and hats) to work with participants to improve their dexterity, mobility, concentration and to lift the mood of your home. The toolkit is made with complete beginners in mind! We will guide you from start to finish.</span></p>'),(4379,491,'_faq_1_answer','field_658489586da98'),(4380,491,'faq_2_question','How can we fit these into a busy schedule?'),(4381,491,'_faq_2_question','field_658489486da97'),(4382,491,'faq_2_answer','<p class=\"Body\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-family: \'Century Gothic\',sans-serif;\">Some of these activities can be delivered on a one-to-one basis in 5 -10mins to encourage interaction between staff and residents and can even be used in people\'s rooms for those that cannot travel down to a communal space. Even just a short session can bring benefits to your staff and the people who live in your home. You could consider scheduling a regular weekly session at the same time each week so that people know when the session is happening.</span></p>'),(4383,491,'_faq_2_answer','field_658489586da98'),(4384,491,'faq','6'),(4385,491,'_faq','field_658489286da96'),(4386,491,'faq_3_question','How long will a session take to run?'),(4387,491,'_faq_3_question','field_658489486da97'),(4388,491,'faq_3_answer','<p class=\"Body\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-family: \'Century Gothic\',sans-serif;\">We suggest a session of 45-60 minutes of uninterrupted circus activity. Ideally, you should allow time before the session whilst people are entering the room and add some time at the end of the session for a gentle warm-down and socialising afterwards.<u></u></span></p>'),(4389,491,'_faq_3_answer','field_658489586da98'),(4390,491,'faq_4_question','Where can I buy circus equipment?'),(4391,491,'_faq_4_question','field_658489486da97'),(4392,491,'faq_4_answer','<p class=\"Body\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-family: \'Century Gothic\',sans-serif;\">We will provide you with links to the websites of circus equipment providers in the UK where you can purchase juggling balls, coloured scarves and flower sticks. You can also use other equipment available from online providers – we also use beach balls, parachutes, gymnastic ribbons and peacock feathers in our sessions. </span></p>'),(4393,491,'_faq_4_answer','field_658489586da98'),(4394,491,'faq_5_question','Why should I introduce circus activities to my care home? '),(4395,491,'_faq_5_question','field_658489486da97'),(4396,491,'faq_5_answer','<ul>\r\n 	<li>Taking part in Circus activities can improve the quality of life for people who live in care homes who may have dementia or a range of physical disabilities</li>\r\n 	<li>Circus activities are beneficial for increasing physical movement, collaboration and alertness, verbal and non-verbal communication, and improving quality of life</li>\r\n 	<li>Circus activities can decrease anxiety and agitation uplifting the mood and feel of the individual or group</li>\r\n 	<li>Circus activities can strengthen social interaction between care staff and the people they are caring for, and bring people who live in care homes together in a shared experience. This is particularly important in terms of redressing the isolation caused by the Covid-19 pandemic</li>\r\n 	<li>Circus equipment is intriguing - the equipment is very tactile and sensory, it is easy to pick up, hold, squeeze and interact with – the bright colours and unusual look make you want to pick up and explore the equipment</li>\r\n 	<li>Circus activities can be scaled up or scaled down to meet the needs of individual participants who may have different levels of mobility. We will show you how to use the different types of equipment and how you can adapt the session to make it easier or more challenging based on the needs of the participants</li>\r\n</ul>'),(4397,491,'_faq_5_answer','field_658489586da98'),(4425,56,'_yoast_wpseo_focuskw','contact us'),(4426,56,'_yoast_wpseo_metadesc','Reach out to us for any questions about the Homemade Circus Digital toolkit - your all-in-one resource for crafting engaging circus sessions.'),(4427,56,'_yoast_wpseo_linkdex','36'),(4428,56,'_yoast_wpseo_estimated-reading-time-minutes','1'),(4429,56,'_yoast_wpseo_wordproof_timestamp',''),(4430,258,'_yoast_wpseo_focuskw','Planning your workshops'),(4431,258,'_yoast_wpseo_metadesc','Learn how to organize a circus workshop with our comprehensive guide. Access template plans, checklists, and playlists to ensure a smooth and engaging session.'),(4432,258,'_yoast_wpseo_linkdex','61'),(4433,258,'_yoast_wpseo_content_score','90'),(4434,258,'_yoast_wpseo_estimated-reading-time-minutes','2'),(4435,258,'_yoast_wpseo_wordproof_timestamp',''),(4436,317,'_yoast_wpseo_focuskw','after your workshop'),(4437,317,'_yoast_wpseo_metadesc','Discover effective ways to wrap up your circus session, leaving participants satisfied and eager for the next one. Take notes on successes and areas for improvement.'),(4438,317,'_yoast_wpseo_linkdex','60'),(4439,317,'_yoast_wpseo_content_score','60'),(4440,317,'_yoast_wpseo_estimated-reading-time-minutes','2'),(4441,317,'_yoast_wpseo_wordproof_timestamp',''),(4442,310,'_yoast_wpseo_focuskw','before your workshop'),(4443,310,'_yoast_wpseo_metadesc','Get ready for a seamless workshop experience. Use our guidance and checklists to ensure you have everything ready for your first circus session.'),(4444,310,'_yoast_wpseo_linkdex','69'),(4445,310,'_yoast_wpseo_content_score','90'),(4446,310,'_yoast_wpseo_estimated-reading-time-minutes','3'),(4447,310,'_yoast_wpseo_wordproof_timestamp',''),(4449,314,'_yoast_wpseo_focuskw','During your workshop'),(4450,314,'_yoast_wpseo_metadesc','Learn how to create a safe, judgement-free space at your circus workshop with our guide. Encourage imperfection and discover effective strategies for a fun and memorable session.'),(4451,314,'_yoast_wpseo_linkdex','69'),(4452,314,'_yoast_wpseo_content_score','30'),(4453,314,'_yoast_wpseo_estimated-reading-time-minutes','4'),(4454,314,'_yoast_wpseo_wordproof_timestamp',''),(4455,495,'footnotes',''),(4456,6,'_yoast_wpseo_focuskw','you\'re signed up'),(4457,6,'_yoast_wpseo_linkdex','28'),(4458,6,'_yoast_wpseo_content_score','90'),(4459,6,'_yoast_wpseo_estimated-reading-time-minutes','1'),(4460,6,'_yoast_wpseo_wordproof_timestamp',''),(4461,42,'_yoast_wpseo_focuskw','welcome to the toolkit'),(4462,42,'_yoast_wpseo_metadesc','Ready for a circus adventure in care homes? Our circus artist Charlene will guide you through the toolkit in this short intro video.'),(4463,42,'_yoast_wpseo_linkdex','46'),(4464,42,'_yoast_wpseo_content_score',