;p=17',0,'acf-post-type','',0),(18,3,'2023-06-30 18:58:47','2023-06-30 18:58:47','<!-- wp:paragraph {\"className\":\"wp-embed-aspect-16-9 wp-has-aspect-ratio\"} -->\n<p class=\"wp-embed-aspect-16-9 wp-has-aspect-ratio\">Juggling Balls&nbsp;are a nice familiar piece of circus equipment that most people will recognise and may have even tried before. They help to improve dexterity and grip strength and throwing and catching the ball will improve focus and reaction times. </p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph {\"className\":\"wp-embed-aspect-16-9 wp-has-aspect-ratio\"} -->\n<p class=\"wp-embed-aspect-16-9 wp-has-aspect-ratio\">This video will show you how to introduce the juggling ball in a group exercise, getting familiar with its texture and how it feels. We will show you how to use the juggling ball with a partner to ensure that those with limited movement can take part, and then we will show you some more advanced exercises, working up to a two-ball juggling pattern for those who want to make things more challenging.&nbsp;&nbsp;<br></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:embed {\"url\":\"https://youtu.be/IodjS7C_B60\",\"type\":\"video\",\"providerNameSlug\":\"youtube\",\"responsive\":true,\"className\":\"wp-embed-aspect-16-9 wp-has-aspect-ratio\"} -->\n<figure class=\"wp-block-embed is-type-video is-provider-youtube wp-block-embed-youtube wp-embed-aspect-16-9 wp-has-aspect-ratio\"><div class=\"wp-block-embed__wrapper\">\nhttps://youtu.be/IodjS7C_B60\n</div></figure>\n<!-- /wp:embed -->\n\n<!-- wp:cover {\"url\":\"http://homemade-circus.local/wp-content/uploads/2023/07/Untitled-design-13-1024x576.png\",\"id\":616,\"dimRatio\":50,\"customOverlayColor\":\"#f2eaf9\",\"isUserOverlayColor\":true,\"focalPoint\":{\"x\":0.5,\"y\":0.5},\"minHeight\":350,\"minHeightUnit\":\"px\",\"isDark\":false,\"sizeSlug\":\"large\",\"style\":{\"color\":{\"duotone\":\"unset\"}},\"layout\":{\"type\":\"constrained\"}} -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-cover is-light\" style=\"min-height:350px\"><img class=\"wp-block-cover__image-background wp-image-616 size-large\" alt=\"\" src=\"http://homemade-circus.local/wp-content/uploads/2023/07/Untitled-design-13-1024x576.png\" style=\"object-position:50% 50%\" data-object-fit=\"cover\" data-object-position=\"50% 50%\"/><span aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"wp-block-cover__background has-background-dim\" style=\"background-color:#f2eaf9\"></span><div class=\"wp-block-cover__inner-container\"><!-- wp:heading -->\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Adapting for Parkinsons:</strong></h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>• <strong>Focus on balance, not throws</strong>: For people with involuntary movements, throwing juggling balls often leads to disappointment, since precise throws and catches are needed to create ball patterns. Instead, focus on balance points, balancing balls on the backs of hands, heads, legs or elbows.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>• <strong>Build strength by squeezing:</strong> try squeezing the balls as if trying to pop them, rolling them up and down the arms, or holding them in an ice cream grip.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p><strong>• Work up to throws slowly:</strong> If you do move onto throwing and catching, start with two-handed throws, or let participants use their stronger hand without changing the activity, then build up to one hand. A good way to start is by throwing the balls as hard as possible onto the floor, or trying to hit the ceiling, before attempting an actual catch.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph --></div></div>\n<!-- /wp:cover -->','Juggling Balls','','publish','closed','closed','','juggling','','','2026-08-20 12:37:40','2026-08-20 12:37:40','',0,'https://homemadecircus.yme.so/?post_type=activity&#038;p=18',0,'activity','',0),(19,1,'2023-06-30 18:51:03','2023-06-30 18:51:03','{\"version\": 2, \"isGlobalStylesUserThemeJSON\": true }','Custom Styles','','publish','closed','closed','','wp-global-styles-twentytwentythree','','','2023-06-30 18:51:03','2023-06-30 18:51:03','',0,'https://homemadecircus.yme.so/wp-global-styles-twentytwentythree/',0,'wp_global_styles','',0),(23,1,'2023-06-30 19:00:17','2023-06-30 19:00:17','<iframe title=\"Upswing SEASONS Live Trailer\" width=\"500\" height=\"281\" src=\"https://www.youtube.com/embed/anUe4v67SiA?feature=oembed\" frameborder=\"0\" allow=\"accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture; web-share\" allowfullscreen></iframe>','','','publish','closed','closed','','25f981b5614adab784433c674998bf9a','','','2023-06-30 19:00:17','2023-06-30 19:00:17','',0,'https://homemadecircus.yme.so/25f981b5614adab784433c674998bf9a/',0,'oembed_cache','',0),(24,1,'2023-06-30 19:01:36','2023-06-30 19:01:36','','Home','','publish','closed','closed','','home','','','2026-04-09 10:53:00','2026-04-09 10:53:00','',0,'https://homemadecircus.yme.so/?page_id=24',0,'page','',0),(26,1,'2023-06-30 19:07:25','2023-06-30 19:07:25','a:8:{s:8:\"location\";a:1:{i:0;a:1:{i:0;a:3:{s:5:\"param\";s:4:\"page\";s:8:\"operator\";s:2:\"==\";s:5:\"value\";s:2:\"24\";}}}s:8:\"position\";s:6:\"normal\";s:5:\"style\";s:7:\"default\";s:15:\"label_placement\";s:3:\"top\";s:21:\"instruction_placement\";s:5:\"label\";s:14:\"hide_on_screen\";s:0:\"\";s:11:\"description\";s:0:\"\";s:12:\"show_in_rest\";i:0;}','Home','home','publish','closed','closed','','group_649f26a368031','','','2023-12-20 13:24:47','2023-12-20 13:24:47','',0,'https://homemadecircus.yme.so/?post_type=acf-field-group&#038;p=26',0,'acf-field-group','',0),(27,1,'2023-06-30 19:07:25','2023-06-30 19:07:25','a:11:{s:10:\"aria-label\";s:0:\"\";s:4:\"type\";s:4:\"text\";s:12:\"instructions\";s:0:\"\";s:8:\"required\";i:0;s:17:\"conditional_logic\";i:0;s:7:\"wrapper\";a:3:{s:5:\"width\";s:0:\"\";s:5:\"class\";s:0:\"\";s:2:\"id\";s:0:\"\";}s:13:\"default_value\";s:10:\"Connection\";s:9:\"maxlength\";s:0:\"\";s:11:\"placeholder\";s:0:\"\";s:7:\"prepend\";s:0:\"\";s:6:\"append\";s:0