26:29','2023-06-30 19:26:29','<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>We\'re so glad you\'re ready to start your circus adventure in care homes with us!  To begin, watch the short video below and our circus artist Charlene will explain how to navigate the toolkit and get the most out of it.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Each activity page includes everything you need to know, like details of where to get the equipment, how long the activity takes and who the activity is suited for. We suggest starting with the \'Coloured Scarves\' activity and working your way down. </p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:embed {\"url\":\"https://youtu.be/hkc5V3amLzg\",\"type\":\"video\",\"providerNameSlug\":\"youtube\",\"responsive\":true,\"className\":\"wp-embed-aspect-16-9 wp-has-aspect-ratio\"} -->\n<figure class=\"wp-block-embed is-type-video is-provider-youtube wp-block-embed-youtube wp-embed-aspect-16-9 wp-has-aspect-ratio\"><div class=\"wp-block-embed__wrapper\">\nhttps://youtu.be/hkc5V3amLzg\n</div></figure>\n<!-- /wp:embed -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p><strong>When you\'re ready, choose an activity from the purple left-hand menu to get started</strong>.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Had a go at some activities already? We would love to hear about your experience! - <a href=\"https://forms.gle/xUfnE8maKFeVGFDH8\">tell us what you thought here</a>.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->','Welcome to the toolkit','','publish','closed','closed','','welcome','','','2024-05-20 20:53:45','2024-05-20 20:53:45','',0,'https://homemadecircus.yme.so/?page_id=42',0,'page','',0),(44,1,'2023-06-30 19:40:19','2023-06-30 19:40:19','<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Click the \'+\' symbol next to any questions you\'d like the answer to. If you have any questions that are not answered below, you can email us at <a href=\"mailto:info@upswing.org.uk\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">info@upswing.org.uk</a></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:spacer {\"height\":\"11px\"} -->\n<div style=\"height:11px\" aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"wp-block-spacer\"></div>\n<!-- /wp:spacer -->\n\n<!-- wp:image {\"id\":484,\"sizeSlug\":\"large\",\"linkDestination\":\"none\"} -->\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large\"><img src=\"https://homemadecircus.yme.so/wp-content/uploads/2024/04/20230313-7R404981-Edit-1-e1714064953940-1024x394.jpg\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-484\"/></figure>\n<!-- /wp:image -->\n\n<!-- wp:spacer {\"height\":\"17px\"} -->\n<div style=\"height:17px\" aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"wp-block-spacer\"></div>\n<!-- /wp:spacer -->','FAQs','','publish','closed','closed','','faqs','','','2024-05-09 13:58:51','2024-05-09 13:58:51','',0,'https://homemadecircus.yme.so/?page_id=44',0,'page','',0),(50,1,'2023-06-30 19:42:47','2023-06-30 19:42:47','a:8:{s:8:\"location\";a:1:{i:0;a:1:{i:0;a:3:{s:5:\"param\";s:12:\"options_page\";s:8:\"operator\";s:2:\"==\";s:5:\"value\";s:11:\"acf-options\";}}}s:8:\"position\";s:6:\"normal\";s:5:\"style\";s:7:\"default\";s:15:\"label_placement\";s:3:\"top\";s:21:\"instruction_placement\";s:5:\"label\";s:14:\"hide_on_screen\";s:0:\"\";s:11:\"description\";s:0:\"\";s:12:\"show_in_rest\";i:0;}','Header Strapline','header-strapline','publish','closed','closed','','group_649f2fda495dd','','','2023-07-15 15:50:29','2023-07-15 15:50:29','',0,'https://homemadecircus.yme.so/?post_type=acf-field-group&#038;p=50',0,'acf-field-group','',0),(51,1,'2023-06-30 19:42:47','2023-06-30 19:42:47','a:11:{s:10:\"aria-label\";s:0:\"\";s:4:\"type\";s:4:\"text\";s:12:\"instructions\";s:0:\"\";s:8:\"required\";i:0;s:17:\"conditional_logic\";i:0;s:7:\"wrapper\";a:3:{s:5:\"width\";s:0:\"\";s:5:\"class\";s:0:\"\";s:2:\"id\";s:0:\"\";}s:13:\"default_value\";s:0:\"\";s:9:\"maxlength\";s:0:\"\";s:11:\"placeholder\";s:0:\"\";s:7:\"prepend\";s:0:\"\";s:6:\"append\";s:0:\"\";}','Strapline','strapline','publish','closed','closed','','field_649f2fda37d54','','','2023-06-30 19:42:47','2023-06-30 19:42:47','',50,'https://homemadecircus.yme.so/?post_type=acf-field&p=51',0,'acf-field','',0),(54,1,'2023-06-30 19:43:43','2023-06-30 19:43:43','','About','','publish','closed','closed','','about','','','2026-04-09 10:49:45','2026-04-09 10:49:45','',0,'https://homemadecircus.yme.so/?page_id=54',0,'page','',0),(55,1,'2023-06-30 19:43:43','2023-06-30 19:43:43','','About','','inherit','closed','closed','','54-revision-v1','','','2023-06-30 19:43:43','2023-06-30 19:43:43','',54,'https://homemadecircus.yme.so/?p=55',0,'revision','',0),(56,1,'2023-06-30 19:43:53','2023-06-30 19:43:53','<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Any questions? Just get in touch with us below! </p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph {\"style\":{\"elements\":{\"link\":{\"color\":{\"text\":\"var:preset|color|black\"}}}},\"textColor\":\"black\"} -->\n<p class=\"has-black-color has-text-color has-link-color\"><strong>This has been an iterative and collaborative process, and we\'d love that to continue. We welcome feedback, or thoughts if you\'ve used any of these offerings.</strong> </p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:wpforms/form-selector {\"clientId\":\"c49e33f2-e44d-42bb-99bf-2bc702f08ffc\",\"formId\":\"239\",\"copyPasteJsonValue\":\"{\\u0022displayTitle\\u0022:false,\\u0022displayDesc\\u0022:false,\\u0022fieldSize\\u0022:\\u0022medium\\u0022,\\u0022fieldBorderRadius\\u0022:\\u00223px\\u0022,\\u0022fieldBackgroundColor\\u0022:\\u0022#ffffff\\u0022,\\u0022fieldBorderColor\\u0022:\\u0022rgba( 0, 0, 0, 0.25 )\\u0022,\\u0022fieldTextColor\\u0022:\\u0022rgba( 0, 0, 0, 0.7 )\\u0022,\\u0022labelSize\\u0022:\\u0022medium\\u0022,\\u0022labelColor\\u0022:\\u0022rgba( 0, 0, 0, 0.85 )\\u0022,\\u0022labelSublabelColor\\u0022:\\u0022rgba( 0, 0, 0, 0.55 )\\u0022,\\u0022labelErrorColor\\u0022:\\u0022#d63637\\u0022,\\u0022buttonSize\\u0022:\\u0022medium\\u0022,\\u0022buttonBorderRadius\\u0022:\\u00223px\\u0022,\\u0022buttonBackgroundColor\\u0022:\\u0022#066aab\\u0022,\\u0022buttonTextColor\\u0022:\\u0022#ffffff\\u0022}\"} /-->','Contact us','','publish','closed','closed','','contact','','','2024-05-20 20:23:29','2024-05-20 20:23:29','',0,'https://homemadecircus.yme.so/?page_id=56',0,'page','',0),(57,1,'2023-06-30 19:43:53','2023-06-30 19:43:53','','Contact','','inherit','closed','closed','','56-revision-v1','','','2023-06-30 19:43:53','2023-06-30 19:43:53','',56,'https://homemadecircus.yme.so/?p=57',0,'revision','',0),(62,3,'2023-07-15 15:56:45','2023-07-15 15:56:45','<!-- wp:paragraph {\"className\":\"wp-embed-aspect-16-9 wp-has-aspect-ratio\"} -->\n<p class=\"wp-embed-aspect-16-9 wp-has-aspect-ratio\">We love using the Coloured Scarves&nbsp;in our workshops because they are so light and easy to use and experiment with! Throwing and catching scarves will strengthen the hand muscles, improve dexterity and hand-eye coordination. They are also great for those who find catching a challenge because they fall more slowly to the ground. </p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph {\"className\":\"wp-embed-aspect-16-9 wp-has-aspect-ratio\"} -->\n<p class=\"wp-embed-aspect-16-9 wp-has-aspect-ratio\">In this video we will introduce the scarves and show you basic juggling patterns for two and three scarves.&nbsp;You can also try playing around with wearing the scarves in different ways. </p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:embed {\"url\":\"https://youtu.be/WegDLCw_HGE\",\"type\":\"video\",\"providerNameSlug\":\"youtube\",\"responsive\":true,\"className\":\"wp-embed-aspect-16-9 wp-has-aspect-ratio\"} -->\n<figure class=\"wp-block-embed is-type-video is-provider-youtube wp-block-embed-youtube wp-embed-aspect-16-9 wp-has-aspect-ratio\"><div class=\"wp-block-embed__wrapper\">\nhttps://youtu.be/WegDLCw_HGE\n</div></figure>\n<!-- /wp:embed -->\n\n<!-- wp:cover {\"url\":\"http://homemade-circus.local/wp-content/uploads/2023/07/Untitled-design-13-1024x576.png\",\"id\":616,\"dimRatio\":50,\"customOverlayColor\":\"#f2eaf9\",\"isUserOverlayColor\":true,\"focalPoint\":{\"x\":0.5,\"y\":0.5},\"minHeight\":289,\"minHeightUnit\":\"px\",\"isDark\":false,\"sizeSlug\":\"large\",\"style\":{\"color\":{\"duotone\":\"unset\"}},\"layout\":{\"type\":\"constrained\"}} -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-cover is-light\" style=\"min-height:289px\"><img class=\"wp-block-cover__image-background wp-image-616 size-large\" alt=\"\" src=\"http://homemade-circus.local/wp-content/uploads/2023/07/Untitled-design-13-1024x576.png\" style=\"object-position:50% 50%\" data-object-fit=\"cover\" data-object-position=\"50% 50%\"/><span aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"wp-block-cover__background has-background-dim\" style=\"background-color:#f2eaf9\"></span><div class=\"wp-block-cover__inner-container\"><!-- wp:heading -->\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Adapting for Parkinsons:</strong></h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>•  <strong>Easy to catch:</strong> these types of scarves are lightweight, move slower through the air and are easier to catch. They work well with people with delayed reaction times or hands that shake, because they allow for easy throwing and catching. A juggling scarf can be caught with an open, downward-facing hand, which means you don\'t need a high level of dexterity to take part. </p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>•<strong> Scrunching for strength:</strong> scrunching of scarves was popular in our sessions, this enabled participants to strengthen their hand muscles and gain some control with a new sensory feel rather than the usual putty.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>• <strong>Prioritise exploration over perfection:</strong> for the part of the activity that involves drawings shapes like circles, squares or pentagons in the air, the real aim is to enjoy the movement and a burst of colour, not a perfect shape. If someone feels self-conscious about not nailing the shape, they can still join in by throwing and waving the scarves to create their own colour explosion.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph --></div></div>\n<!-- /wp:cover -->','Coloured Scarves','','publish','closed','closed','','coloured-scarves','','','2026-08-20 12:01:57','2026-08-20 12:01:57','',0,'https://homemadecircus.yme.so/?post_type=activity&#038;p=62',0,'activity','',0),(63,3,'2023-07-15 15:56:59','2023-07-15 15:56:59','<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Flower Sticks&nbsp;are designed to be soft enough to hold and squeeze, so the movements in this activity can really help with improving muscle strength. Flower Sticks can be used from a seated or a standing position and are great for promoting social interaction between partners as you roll the stick between you. Adding control sticks to the movement will make it easier and more comfortable for people who have reduced mobility. </p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>We will show you how you can use the Flower Stick on your own or with a partner.&nbsp;Once you get more confident you can challenge yourself to learn tricks with the Flower Stick which will improve your concentration and hand-eye coordination.&nbsp;</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:embed {\"url\":\"https://youtu.be/_9_tSOO0ZWo\",\"type\":\"video\",\"providerNameSlug\":\"youtube\",\"responsive\":true,\"className\":\"wp-embed-aspect-16-9 wp-has-aspect-ratio\"} -->\n<figure class=\"wp-block-embed is-type-video is-provider-youtube wp-block-embed-youtube wp-embed-aspect-16-9 wp-has-aspect-ratio\"><div class=\"wp-block-embed__wrapper\">\nhttps://youtu.be/_9_tSOO0ZWo\n</div></figure>\n<!-- /wp:embed -->\n\n<!-- wp:cover {\"url\":\"http://homemade-circus.local/wp-content/uploads/2023/07/Untitled-design-13-1024x576.png\",\"id\":616,\"dimRatio\":50,\"customOverlayColor\":\"#f2eaf9\",\"isUserOverlayColor\":true,\"focalPoint\":{\"x\":0.5,\"y\":0.5},\"minHeight\":220,\"minHeightUnit\":\"px\",\"isDark\":false,\"sizeSlug\":\"large\",\"style\":{\"color\":{\"duotone\":\"unset\"}},\"layout\":{\"type\":\"constrained\"}} -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-cover is-light\" style=\"min-height:220px\"><img class=\"wp-block-cover__image-background wp-image-616 size-large\" alt=\"\" src=\"http://homemade-circus.local/wp-content/uploads/2023/07/Untitled-design-13-1024x576.png\" style=\"object-position:50% 50%\" data-object-fit=\"cover\" data-object-position=\"50% 50%\"/><span aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"wp-block-cover__background has-background-dim\" style=\"background-color:#f2eaf9\"></span><div class=\"wp-block-cover__inner-container\"><!-- wp:heading -->\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Adapting for Parkinsons:</strong></h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>• <strong>One stick per person:</strong> When each participant works their own flower stick individually, they can move at their own pace, which naturally allows room for involuntary movements. The rubber grip is forgiving, so moves don\'t need to be precise to work, and teaching a wide grip gives extra stability.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>• <strong>Work individually, rather than sharing:</strong> Give each person their own pair of control sticks, rather than sharing a set. This means if someone\'s hand tremors mid-activity, they can pause and let it pass while the other person keeps going with their own sticks, so the activity doesn\'t have to stop for either of them. Sharing one set between two people can make a tremor from either side send the flower stick bouncing unpredictably near both faces, which tends to unsettle people rather than reassure them.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph --></div></div>\n<!-- /wp:cover -->','Flower Sticks','','publish','closed','closed','','flower-sticks','','','2026-08-20 12:37:10','2026-08-20 12:37:10','',0,'https://homemadecircus.yme.so/?post_type=activity&#038;p=63',0,'activity','',0),(64,3,'2023-07-15 15:57:13','2023-07-15 15:57:13','<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Peacock Feathers&nbsp;are&nbsp;a great piece of equipment because you can explore the colours and the texture of the feathers. </p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>You can use the feather to brush your hands or your face and they\'re a great conversation starter as you can ask people to describe how it feels, or what colours they can see. Flicking the feather up and catching it as it floats also helps to improve attention and focus. Balancing the feather on different parts of your body will work core muscles and stability.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>We will also show you how you can work together to make the activity easier until your participants feel more confident about balancing the feather on their own. &nbsp;</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:embed {\"url\":\"https://youtu.be/q1IApcqqxWA\",\"type\":\"video\",\"providerNameSlug\":\"youtube\",\"responsive\":true,\"className\":\"wp-embed-aspect-16-9 wp-has-aspect-ratio\"} -->\n<figure class=\"wp-block-embed is-type-video is-provider-youtube wp-block-embed-youtube wp-embed-aspect-16-9 wp-has-aspect-ratio\"><div class=\"wp-block-embed__wrapper\">\nhttps://youtu.be/q1IApcqqxWA\n</div></figure>\n<!-- /wp:embed -->\n\n<!-- wp:cover {\"url\":\"http://homemade-circus.local/wp-content/uploads/2023/07/Untitled-design-13-1024x576.png\",\"id\":616,\"dimRatio\":50,\"customOverlayColor\":\"#f2eaf9\",\"isUserOverlayColor\":true,\"focalPoint\":{\"x\":0.5,\"y\":0.5},\"minHeight\":220,\"minHeightUnit\":\"px\",\"isDark\":false,\"sizeSlug\":\"large\",\"style\":{\"color\":{\"duotone\":\"unset\"}},\"layout\":{\"type\":\"constrained\"}} -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-cover is-light\" style=\"min-height:220px\"><img class=\"wp-block-cover__image-background wp-image-616 size-large\" alt=\"\" src=\"http://homemade-circus.local/wp-content/uploads/2023/07/Untitled-design-13-1024x576.png\" style=\"object-position:50% 50%\" data-object-fit=\"cover\" data-object-position=\"50% 50%\"/><span aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"wp-block-cover__background has-background-dim\" style=\"background-color:#f2eaf9\"></span><div class=\"wp-block-cover__inner-container\"><!-- wp:heading -->\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Adapting for Parkinsons:</strong></h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>• <strong>Forgiving for movement:</strong> feathers have a flex in the main body which acts as a stabiliser, much like a suspension in a car smoothing out bumps in the road. The feather compensates for any involuntary shakes in the hand, which allows people with Parkinsons to still develop the skill of balancing.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>• <strong>Ask, don\'t assume:</strong> most people taking part will know their own bodies well, so listening to them about which hand or body part they want to balance on can lead to better results. If they are having success with one side of the body, you can encourage them to try the other side if they\'d like more of a challenge.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph --></div></div>\n<!-- /wp:cover -->','Peacock Feathers','','publish','closed','closed','','peacock-feathers','','','2026-08-20 12:36:35','2026-08-20 12:36:35','',0,'https://homemadecircus.yme.so/?post_type=activity&#038;p=64',0,'activity','',0),(65,3,'2023-07-15 15:57:25','2023-07-15 15:57:25','<!-- wp:paragraph {\"className\":\"wp-embed-aspect-16-9 wp-has-aspect-ratio\"} -->\n<p class=\"wp-embed-aspect-16-9 wp-has-aspect-ratio\">Hats&nbsp;are a lot of fun and can be used really effectively in partner or group work and as a conversation starter. They are a very accessible piece of equipment which can easily be adapted for everyone to use, even for those with low mobility. </p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph {\"className\":\"wp-embed-aspect-16-9 wp-has-aspect-ratio\"} -->\n<p class=\"wp-embed-aspect-16-9 wp-has-aspect-ratio\">In this session we\'ll show you how you can balance the hat on different parts of your body such as your fist, elbow or shoulder. This can help with concentration and balancing skills. You can also use the hats to improvise with the group, tipping your hat to other people in the session. Once you feel more&nbsp;confident&nbsp;we will teach you a basic hat tumbling trick which will improve your coordination skills.&nbsp;</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:embed {\"url\":\"https://youtu.be/WRvChy3HvfQ\",\"type\":\"video\",\"providerNameSlug\":\"youtube\",\"responsive\":true,\"className\":\"wp-embed-aspect-16-9 wp-has-aspect-ratio\"} -->\n<figure class=\"wp-block-embed is-type-video is-provider-youtube wp-block-embed-youtube wp-embed-aspect-16-9 wp-has-aspect-ratio\"><div class=\"wp-block-embed__wrapper\">\nhttps://youtu.be/WRvChy3HvfQ\n</div></figure>\n<!-- /wp:embed -->\n\n<!-- wp:cover {\"url\":\"http://homemade-circus.local/wp-content/uploads/2023/07/Untitled-design-13-1024x576.png\",\"id\":616,\"dimRatio\":50,\"customOverlayColor\":\"#f2eaf9\",\"isUserOverlayColor\":true,\"focalPoint\":{\"x\":0.5,\"y\":0.5},\"minHeight\":169,\"minHeightUnit\":\"px\",\"isDark\":false,\"sizeSlug\":\"large\",\"style\":{\"color\":{\"duotone\":\"unset\"}},\"layout\":{\"type\":\"constrained\"}} -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-cover is-light\" style=\"min-height:169px\"><img class=\"wp-block-cover__image-background wp-image-616 size-large\" alt=\"\" src=\"http://homemade-circus.local/wp-content/uploads/2023/07/Untitled-design-13-1024x576.png\" style=\"object-position:50% 50%\" data-object-fit=\"cover\" data-object-position=\"50% 50%\"/><span aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"wp-block-cover__background has-background-dim\" style=\"background-color:#f2eaf9\"></span><div class=\"wp-block-cover__inner-container\"><!-- wp:heading -->\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Adapting for Parkinsons:</strong></h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>•<strong> Balance at their own pace</strong>: hats give a stable balance that resists tremors and shakes, and can be worked at each participant\'s own pace. Taking a hat on and off is a multi-step process that can be completed in the participant\'s own time.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph --></div></div>\n<!-- /wp:cover -->','Hats','','publish','closed','closed','','hats','','','2026-08-20 12:36:20','2026-08-20 12:36:20','',0,'https://homemadecircus.yme.so/?post_type=activity&#038;p=65',0,'activity','',0),(71,1,'2023-07-15 16:00:16','2023-07-15 16:00:16','','Contact us','','inherit','closed','closed','','56-revision-v1','','','2023-07-15 16:00:16','2023-07-15 16:00:16','',56,'https://homemadecircus.yme.so/?p=71',0,'revision','',0),(110,1,'2023-07-15 18:33:55','2023-07-15 18:33:55','<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>this is the contact us page</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->','Contact us','','inherit','closed','closed','','56-revision-v1','','','2023-07-15 18:33:55','2023-07-15 18:33:55','',56,'https://homemadecircus.yme.so/?p=110',0,'revision','',0),(113,1,'2023-07-24 14:11:33','2023-07-24 14:11:33','{{unknown}}','','','publish','closed','closed','','94e77044598a0f40fdcebe0cced7c3bf','','','2023-07-24 14:11:33','2023-07-24 14:11:33','',0,'https://homemadecircus.yme.so/94e77044598a0f40fdcebe0cced7c3bf/',0,'oembed_cache','',0),(119,1,'2023-07-24 16:38:13','2023-07-24 16:38:13','a:8:{s:8:\"location\";a:1:{i:0;a:1:{i:0;a:3:{s:5:\"param\";s:12:\"options_page\";s:8:\"operator\";s:2:\"==\";s:5:\"value\";s:11:\"acf-options\";}}}s:8:\"position\";s:6:\"normal\";s:5:\"style\";s:7:\"default\";s:15:\"label_placement\";s:3:\"top\";s:21:\"instruction_placement\";s:5:\"label\";s:14:\"hide_on_screen\";s:0:\"\";s:11:\"description\";s:0:\"\";s:12:\"show_in_rest\";i:0;}','Footer','footer','publish','closed','closed','','group_64bea8ddb570c','','','2023-07-24 16:38:13','2023-07-24 16:38:13','',0,'https://homemadecircus.yme.so/?post_type=acf-field-group&#038;p=119',0,'acf-field-group','',0),(120,1,'2023-07-24 16:38:13','2023-07-24 16:38:13','a:11:{s:10:\"aria-label\";s:0:\"\";s:4:\"type\";s:7:\"wysiwyg\";s:12:\"instructions\";s:0:\"\";s:8:\"required\";i:0;s:17:\"conditional_logic\";i:0;s:7:\"wrapper\";a:3:{s:5:\"width\";s:0:\"\";s:5:\"class\";s:0:\"\";s:2:\"id\";s:0:\"\";}s:13:\"default_value\";s:0:\"\";s:4:\"tabs\";s:3:\"all\";s:7:\"toolbar\";s:4:\"full\";s:12:\"media_upload\";i:1;s:5:\"delay\";i:0;}','footer','footer','publish','closed','closed','','field_64bea8dede5c8','','','2023-07-24 16:38:13','2023-07-24 16:38:13','',119,'https://homemadecircus.yme.so/?post_type=acf-field&p=120',0,'acf-field','',0),(121,1,'2023-07-24 16:50:35','2023-07-24 16:50:35','<!-- wp:heading -->\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Who we are</h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p><strong class=\"privacy-policy-tutorial\">Suggested text: </strong>Our website address is: https://homemadecircus.yme.so.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading -->\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Comments</h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p><strong class=\"privacy-policy-tutorial\">Suggested text: </strong>When visitors leave comments on the site we collect the data shown in the comments form, and also the visitor’s IP address and browser user agent string to help spam detection.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>An anonymized string created from your email address (also called a hash) may be provided to the Gravatar service to see if you are using it. The Gravatar service privacy policy is available here: https://automattic.com/privacy/. After approval of your comment, your profile picture is visible to the public in the context of your comment.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading -->\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Media</h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p><strong class=\"privacy-policy-tutorial\">Suggested text: </strong>If you upload images to the website, you should avoid uploading images with embedded location data (EXIF GPS) included. Visitors to the website can download and extract any location data from images on the website.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading -->\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Cookies</h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p><strong class=\"privacy-policy-tutorial\">Suggested text: </strong>If you leave a comment on our site you may opt-in to saving your name, email address and website in cookies. These are for your convenience so that you do not have to fill in your details again when you leave another comment. These cookies will last for one year.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>If you visit our login page, we will set a temporary cookie to determine if your browser accepts cookies. This cookie contains no personal data and is discarded when you close your browser.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>When you log in, we will also set up several cookies to save your login information and your screen display choices. Login cookies last for two days, and screen options cookies last for a year. If you select \"Remember Me\", your login will persist for two weeks. If you log out of your account, the login cookies will be removed.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>If you edit or publish an article, an additional cookie will be saved in your browser. This cookie includes no personal data and simply indicates the post ID of the article you just edited. It expires after 1 day.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading -->\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Embedded content from other websites</h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p><strong class=\"privacy-policy-tutorial\">Suggested text: </strong>Articles on this site may include embedded content (e.g. videos, images, articles, etc.). Embedded content from other websites behaves in the exact same way as if the visitor has visited the other website.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>These websites may collect data about you, use cookies, embed additional third-party tracking, and monitor your interaction with that embedded content, including tracking your interaction with the embedded content if you have an account and are logged in to that website.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading -->\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Who we share your data with</h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p><strong class=\"privacy-policy-tutorial\">Suggested text: </strong>If you request a password reset, your IP address will be included in the reset email.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading -->\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">How long we retain your data</h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p><strong class=\"privacy-policy-tutorial\">Suggested text: </strong>If you leave a comment, the comment and its metadata are retained indefinitely. This is so we can recognize and approve any follow-up comments automatically instead of holding them in a moderation queue.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>For users that register on our website (if any), we also store the personal information they provide in their user profile. All users can see, edit, or delete their personal information at any time (except they cannot change their username). Website administrators can also see and edit that information.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading -->\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">What rights you have over your data</h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p><strong class=\"privacy-policy-tutorial\">Suggested text: </strong>If you have an account on this site, or have left comments, you can request to receive an exported file of the personal data we hold about you, including any data you have provided to us. You can also request that we erase any personal data we hold about you. This does not include any data we are obliged to keep for administrative, legal, or security purposes.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading -->\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Where your data is sent</h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p><strong class=\"privacy-policy-tutorial\">Suggested text: </strong>Visitor comments may be checked through an automated spam detection service.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->','Privacy Policy','','inherit','closed','closed','','3-revision-v1','','','2023-07-24 16:50:35','2023-07-24 16:50:35','',3,'https://homemadecircus.yme.so/?p=121',0,'revision','',0),(124,1,'2023-07-24 17:04:30','2023-07-24 17:04:30','','Supporter Membership','','publish','closed','closed','','general-membership','','','2026-04-09 10:55:36','2026-04-09 10:55:36','',0,'https://homemadecircus.yme.so/?post_type=memberpressproduct&#038;p=124',0,'memberpressproduct','',0),(125,1,'2024-05-20 11:59:29','2023-07-25 10:51:04','','Log In|Log Out','','publish','closed','closed','','log-inlog-out','','','2024-05-20 11:59:29','2024-05-20 11:59:29','',0,'https://homemadecircus.yme.so/?p=125',4,'nav_menu_item','',0),(126,1,'2024-09-09 14:39:07','2023-07-25 10:59:06','','Contact','','publish','closed','closed','','contact','','','2024-09-09 14:39:07','2024-09-09 14:39:07','',0,'https://homemadecircus.yme.so/?p=126',2,'nav_menu_item','',0),(127,1,'2024-09-09 14:39:07','2023-07-25 10:59:06','','About','','publish','closed','closed','','about','','','2024-09-09 14:39:07','2024-09-09 14:39:07','',0,'https://homemadecircus.yme.so/?p=127',1,'nav_menu_item','',0),(128,1,'2024-09-09 14:39:07','2023-07-25 10:59:06','','Log In|Log Out','','publish','closed','closed','','log-inlog-out-2','','','2024-09-09 14:39:07','2024-09-09 14:39:07','',0,'https://homemadecircus.yme.so/?p=128',4,'nav_menu_item','',0),(137,1,'2023-07-25 11:48:55','2023-07-25 11:48:55','','Partial:','','publish','closed','closed','','partial','','','2024-06-03 16:50:04','2024-06-03 16:50:04','',0,'https://homemadecircus.yme.so/?post_type=memberpressrule&#038;p=137',0,'memberpressrule','',0),(140,1,'2024-05-20 11:59:29','2023-07-25 14:16:53','','Members','','publish','closed','closed','','140','','','2024-05-20 11:59:29','2024-05-20 11:59:29','',0,'https://homemadecircus.yme.so/?p=140',1,'nav_menu_item','',0),(147,1,'2023-07-25 14:32:15','0000-00-00 00:00:00','','Snippet Preview','','draft','closed','closed','','xyz