-->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph {\"align\":\"left\"} -->\n<p class=\"has-text-align-left\"><a href=\"https://homemadecircus.yme.so/planning-your-workshop/health-and-safety/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Health &amp; Safety</a></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph --></div>\n<!-- /wp:column -->\n\n<!-- wp:column -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-column\"><!-- wp:image {\"id\":274,\"width\":\"337px\",\"height\":\"auto\",\"sizeSlug\":\"full\",\"linkDestination\":\"custom\"} -->\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-full is-resized\"><a href=\"https://homemadecircus.yme.so/before-your-workshop/\"><img src=\"https://homemadecircus.yme.so/wp-content/uploads/2023/10/HEALTH-SAFETY-6.png\" alt=\"Before your workshop\" class=\"wp-image-274\" style=\"width:337px;height:auto\"/></a></figure>\n<!-- /wp:image -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph {\"align\":\"left\"} -->\n<p class=\"has-text-align-left\"><a href=\"https://homemadecircus.yme.so/planning-your-workshop/before-your-workshop/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Before Your Workshop</a></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph --></div>\n<!-- /wp:column --></div>\n<!-- /wp:columns -->\n\n<!-- wp:spacer {\"height\":\"14px\"} -->\n<div style=\"height:14px\" aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"wp-block-spacer\"></div>\n<!-- /wp:spacer -->\n\n<!-- wp:columns -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-columns\"><!-- wp:column -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-column\"><!-- wp:image {\"id\":277,\"width\":\"350px\",\"height\":\"auto\",\"sizeSlug\":\"full\",\"linkDestination\":\"custom\"} -->\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-full is-resized\"><a href=\"https://homemadecircus.yme.so/during-your-workshop/\"><img src=\"https://homemadecircus.yme.so/wp-content/uploads/2023/10/HEALTH-SAFETY-9.png\" alt=\"During your workshop\" class=\"wp-image-277\" style=\"width:350px;height:auto\"/></a></figure>\n<!-- /wp:image -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph {\"align\":\"left\"} -->\n<p class=\"has-text-align-left\"><a href=\"https://homemadecircus.yme.so/planning-your-workshop/during-your-workshop/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">During Your Workshop</a></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph --></div>\n<!-- /wp:column -->\n\n<!-- wp:column -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-column\"><!-- wp:image {\"id\":293,\"width\":\"352px\",\"height\":\"auto\",\"sizeSlug\":\"full\",\"linkDestination\":\"custom\"} -->\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-full is-resized\"><a href=\"https://homemadecircus.yme.so/after-your-workshop/\"><img src=\"https://homemadecircus.yme.so/wp-content/uploads/2023/10/HEALTH-SAFETY-11.png\" alt=\"After your workshop\" class=\"wp-image-293\" style=\"width:352px;height:auto\"/></a></figure>\n<!-- /wp:image -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph {\"align\":\"left\"} -->\n<p class=\"has-text-align-left\"><a href=\"https://homemadecircus.yme.so/planning-your-workshop/after-your-workshop/\">After Your Workshop</a></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph --></div>\n<!-- /wp:column --></div>\n<!-- /wp:columns -->','Planning Your Workshop','','inherit','closed','closed','','258-revision-v1','','','2024-03-04 17:30:54','2024-03-04 17:30:54','',258,'https://homemadecircus.yme.so/?p=386',0,'revision','',0),(388,3,'2024-03-04 17:35:14','2024-03-04 17:35:14','<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p><strong>As always, health and safety is an important consideration, especially when using new equipment. Some exercises involve touch and we always want to make sure everyone we’re working with feels completely comfortable with all parts of the activity. Follow these steps to make sure you have all the necessary Health and Safety in place before your session:</strong></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:list -->\n<ul><!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>Make sure you fill out a risk assessment form before your workshop. You can use our template which can be found in the \'Useful Links\' section on the right-hand side of this page.<br></li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>Be sure that you have enough care home staff in the room at all times. Ideally you need 2-3 care home staff working alongside you to support you in delivering the session. Brief them on the activities, structure and Health and Safety considerations beforehand.<br></li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>Check that each participant or resident has enough space to stretch their arms and legs without clashing.<br></li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>Leave space for people to exit and enter the workshop circle without disturbing the rest of the participants.<br></li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>If using touch in your session, let the person know what you are planning to do and ask their permission before you touch them. For example, when using a Flower Stick to massage each others\' hands and arms, you can say \'If you want, we can try using the sticks to gently massage your arms and hands, would you be okay with that?\'. <br></li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>If you’re assisting someone in moving a part of their body you can also check with them that it feels ok and nothing is painful.<br></li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>Ensure you always do a light warm-up and cool-down before and after every sessions so that no one gets hurt.<br></li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item --></ul>\n<!-- /wp:list -->','Health and Safety','','inherit','closed','closed','','306-revision-v1','','','2024-03-04 17:35:14','2024-03-04 17:35:14','',306,'https://homemadecircus.yme.so/?p=388',0,'revision','',0),(391,3,'2024-03-04 17:43:00','2024-03-04 17:43:00','<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p><strong>Being organised and prepared before facilitating your workshop will help it run smoothly. Use the \'Workshop Checklist\' provided under \'Useful Links\' to confirm you have all necessary materials to start. </strong></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>That being said, the playful essence of these workshops means surprises can occur. Stay flexible, improvise when needed and most importantly, have fun - the more you run these sessions, the more comfortable you\'ll become handling unexpected developments.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading -->\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Music:</strong></h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Circus activities work well when there is music playing. It helps loosen everyone up and direct the energy of the room. Head to our Spotify page to check out the playlists we\'ve set up to suit various moods. You can find the link under \'Useful Links\' in the right-hand side of this page. </p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading -->\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Things to consider with music:</strong></h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:list -->\n<ul><!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>Is the volume suitable for the group</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>We recommend using music without words (instrumental) during activities when giving instructions. This is crucial for helping people to focus on what you\'re saying</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>What type of music are you playing to set the mood? We like to choose tracks which are bright and uplifting</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>Music is a powerful way of connecting with people who are living with dementia. We’ve witnessed some amazing reactions when someone dementia hears their favourite song. Spend some time finding out what kind of music your participants are interested in. You could then curate a playlist for the participants based on their own musical tastes or favourite songs - which really helps with engagement and community-building.</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>Sometimes it may be hard find this out from the participants so remember to ask your colleagues as they may have more knowledge about an individual’s needs, likes and dislikes</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item --></ul>\n<!-- /wp:list -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading -->\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Setting up the room:</strong></h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:list -->\n<ul><!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>Choose a large, well-lit comfortable room where you will not be interrupted, and set up the chairs in a large circle with space between each chair. This is important so that participants have room to extend their arms and use the equipment without bumping into one another. Make sure there is an open space at the centre of the circle for you to stand when delivering instructions and for the participants to see everyone else across the circle</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>Ensure there are chairs set up in the circle for colleagues, assistants or visitors so that everyone is included</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>Switch off any TV or radio </li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>Start your music just before the session to set the mood</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>Introduce yourself and the other people who are leading the workshop. You might want to ask everyone in the circle to say their name and others to respond by giving them a verbal hello or smile or a wave back</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>Start the workshop with some introductory games, to connect with the participants whilst the other participants are arriving.&nbsp;Once everyone is in the room commence with an essential physical warm up to ensure safe delivery</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item --></ul>\n<!-- /wp:list -->','Before your Workshop','','inherit','closed','closed','','310-revision-v1','','','2024-03-04 17:43:00','2024-03-04 17:43:00','',310,'https://homemadecircus.yme.so/?p=391',0,'revision','',0),(393,3,'2024-03-04 17:52:11','2024-03-04 17:52:11','<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>It is nice to round-off the activities after you are finished so that everyone is left feeling content and the connected feeling continues. It is also a great time to take notes for yourself of what did and didn\'t work, so that you can focus on those in the next session. Here are some ideas of ways to close the session that will leave participants excited for the next one, choose what feels right for the room:</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:list -->\n<ul><!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>Cooldown</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>If the atmosphere seems lively, you can keep the music playing and use this as socialising time</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>Serving tea &amp; cake whilst everyone’s together</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>Remind people when the next session is while they’re in the room</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>If you’re keeping records of people’s attendance and any surprising interactions you noticed, it’s a great time to immediately write this up straight after while you remember – We’d love to hear about your experience so it’s also a good time to send us any feedback at <a href=\"mailto:info@upswing.org.uk\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">info@upswing.org.uk</a>, we would love to hear from you! </li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item --></ul>\n<!-- /wp:list -->','After your Workshop','','inherit','closed','closed','','317-revision-v1','','','2024-03-04 17:52:11','2024-03-04 17:52:11','',317,'https://homemadecircus.yme.so/?p=393',0,'revision','',0),(394,3,'2024-03-04 17:53:34','2024-03-04 17:53:34','<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>It is nice to round-off the activities after you are finished so that everyone is left feeling content and the connected feeling continues. It is also a great time to take notes for yourself of what did and didn\'t work, so that you can focus on those in the next session. Here are some ideas of ways to close the session that will leave participants excited for the next one, choose what feels right for the room:</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:list -->\n<ul><!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>Cooldown</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>If the atmosphere seems lively, you can keep the music playing and use this as socialising time</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>Serving tea &amp; cake whilst everyone’s together</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>Remind people when the next session is while they’re in the room</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>If you’re keeping records of people’s attendance and any surprising interactions you noticed, it’s a great time to immediately write this up straight after while you remember</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>We’d love to hear about your experience so it’s also a good time to send us any feedback at <a href=\"mailto:info@upswing.org.uk\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">info@upswing.org.uk</a>, we would appreciate any thoughts you had about the Digital toolkit, it\'s content or how your sessions are going</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item --></ul>\n<!-- /wp:list -->','After your Workshop','','inherit','closed','closed','','317-revision-v1','','','2024-03-04 17:53:34','2024-03-04 17:53:34','',317,'https://homemadecircus.yme.so/?p=394',0,'revision','',0),(408,3,'2024-03-19 13:48:38','2024-03-19 13:48:38','<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Blocks may look like an unusual piece of circus equipment but these blocks are lightweight, colourful and easy to hold. Using them can aid dexterity, coordination and strength.&nbsp;&nbsp;</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>In this video we will show you exercises using one or two blocks depending on mobility. For more of a challenge we\'ll walk you through an exercise using pressure to move the blocks, alongside a partner or a larger group.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>We’ve found that blocks are one of the most popular pieces of equipment in our circus workshops. There’s so much you can do with them and we’ve included some of our favourite games in the video. See what ideas you can come up with!</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:embed {\"url\":\"https://youtu.be/rA6ZpJZHdy4\",\"type\":\"video\",\"providerNameSlug\":\"youtube\",\"responsive\":true,\"className\":\"wp-embed-aspect-16-9 wp-has-aspect-ratio\"} -->\n<figure class=\"wp-block-embed is-type-video is-provider-youtube wp-block-embed-youtube wp-embed-aspect-16-9 wp-has-aspect-ratio\"><div class=\"wp-block-embed__wrapper\">\nhttps://youtu.be/rA6ZpJZHdy4\n</div></figure>\n<!-- /wp:embed -->\n\n<!-- wp:cover {\"url\":\"http://homemade-circus.local/wp-content/uploads/2023/07/Untitled-design-13-1024x576.png\",\"id\":616,\"dimRatio\":50,\"customOverlayColor\":\"#f2eaf9\",\"isUserOverlayColor\":true,\"focalPoint\":{\"x\":0.5,\"y\":0.5},\"minHeight\":350,\"minHeightUnit\":\"px\",\"isDark\":false,\"sizeSlug\":\"large\",\"style\":{\"color\":{\"duotone\":\"unset\"}},\"layout\":{\"type\":\"constrained\"}} -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-cover is-light\" style=\"min-height:350px\"><img class=\"wp-block-cover__image-background wp-image-616 size-large\" alt=\"\" src=\"http://homemade-circus.local/wp-content/uploads/2023/07/Untitled-design-13-1024x576.png\" style=\"object-position:50% 50%\" data-object-fit=\"cover\" data-object-position=\"50% 50%\"/><span aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"wp-block-cover__background has-background-dim\" style=\"background-color:#f2eaf9\"></span><div class=\"wp-block-cover__inner-container\"><!-- wp:heading -->\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Adapting for Parkinsons:</strong></h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>• <strong>Work with involuntary movement, not against it</strong>: blocks are great for people with involuntary movement. Most block activities can start with two hands before building up to using just one. This lets participants compensate for involuntary movements by using one hand to support the other. If the pressure between hands drops and the block falls, there\'s no damage or risk of injury.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>• <strong>Try stacking and balancing:</strong> you can focus on stacking and balancing multiple blocks, holding pressure between two blocks (or three or four in a line, in pairs), along with work on isolations and intentional movement while gripping the blocks.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>•  <strong>Encourage stillness and intentional motion: </strong>we developed this exercise further into practicing stillness. You can balance a block on the head while isolating another block in front of the body.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph --></div></div>\n<!-- /wp:cover -->','Blocks','','publish','closed','closed','','blocks','','','2026-08-20 12:35:11','2026-08-20 12:35:11','',0,'https://homemadecircus.yme.so/?post_type=activity&#038;p=408',0,'activity','',0),(410,3,'2024-03-11 14:29:26','2024-03-11 14:29:26','','BLOCKS - Activity Info Sheet - Homemade Circus','','inherit','open','closed','','blocks-activity-info-sheet-homemade-circus','','','2024-03-19 13:48:39','2024-03-19 13:48:39','',408,'https://homemadecircus.yme.so/wp-content/uploads/2024/03/BLOCKS-Activity-Info-Sheet-Homemade-Circus.pdf',0,'attachment','application/pdf',0),(411,3,'2024-03-19 13:57:25','2024-03-19 13:57:25','<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Colourful bunting is lightweight and versatile. We pass a string of bunting around the circle at the start of every workshop. It’s a great way to draw people into the session and create connections across the group.&nbsp;</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>In this video we will show you how you can use the bunting to get everyone engaged with the workshop, regardless of their level of mobility. We’ll demonstrate some fun activities you can do with the bunting in order to get your circus workshop off to a great start.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:embed {\"url\":\"https://youtu.be/zvaf781IhAI\",\"type\":\"video\",\"providerNameSlug\":\"youtube\",\"responsive\":true,\"className\":\"wp-embed-aspect-16-9 wp-has-aspect-ratio\"} -->\n<figure class=\"wp-block-embed is-type-video is-provider-youtube wp-block-embed-youtube wp-embed-aspect-16-9 wp-has-aspect-ratio\"><div class=\"wp-block-embed__wrapper\">\nhttps://youtu.be/zvaf781IhAI\n</div></figure>\n<!-- /wp:embed -->','Bunting','','publish','closed','closed','','bunting','','','2024-05-09 12:38:13','2024-05-09 12:38:13','',0,'https://homemadecircus.yme.so/?post_type=activity&#038;p=411',0,'activity','',0),(412,3,'2024-03-11 14:32:49','2024-03-11 14:32:49','','BUNTING - Activity Info Sheet - Homemade Circus','','inherit','open','closed','','bunting-activity-info-sheet-homemade-circus','','','2024-03-19 13:57:26','2024-03-19 13:57:26','',411,'https://homemadecircus.yme.so/wp-content/uploads/2024/03/BUNTING-Activity-Info-Sheet-Homemade-Circus.pdf',0,'attachment','application/pdf',0),(413,3,'2024-03-19 13:42:28','2024-03-19 13:42:28','<!-- wp:paragraph {\"className\":\"wp-embed-aspect-16-9 wp-has-aspect-ratio\"} -->\n<p class=\"wp-embed-aspect-16-9 wp-has-aspect-ratio\">We use beach balls as people are entering the workshop and joining the circle. Gently throwing and catching (or bouncing) a beach ball will get people engaged whilst you are waiting for everyone to join. You can add two or three beach balls to the circle if people are feeling confident. </p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph {\"className\":\"wp-embed-aspect-16-9 wp-has-aspect-ratio\"} -->\n<p class=\"wp-embed-aspect-16-9 wp-has-aspect-ratio\">This activity is great for improving focus and hand-eye coordination and helps develop connections amongst the group. In this video we’ll show you ways to get your workshop off to a great start!</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:embed {\"url\":\"https://youtu.be/urWBElsszqY\",\"type\":\"video\",\"providerNameSlug\":\"youtube\",\"responsive\":true,\"className\":\"wp-embed-aspect-16-9 wp-has-aspect-ratio\"} -->\n<figure class=\"wp-block-embed is-type-video is-provider-youtube wp-block-embed-youtube wp-embed-aspect-16-9 wp-has-aspect-ratio\"><div class=\"wp-block-embed__wrapper\">\nhttps://youtu.be/urWBElsszqY\n</div></figure>\n<!-- /wp:embed -->\n\n<!-- wp:cover {\"url\":\"http://homemade-circus.local/wp-content/uploads/2023/07/Untitled-design-13-1024x576.png\",\"id\":616,\"dimRatio\":50,\"customOverlayColor\":\"#f2eaf9\",\"isUserOverlayColor\":true,\"focalPoint\":{\"x\":0.5,\"y\":0.5},\"minHeight\":199,\"minHeightUnit\":\"px\",\"isDark\":false,\"sizeSlug\":\"large\",\"style\":{\"color\":{\"duotone\":\"unset\"}},\"layout\":{\"type\":\"constrained\"}} -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-cover is-light\" style=\"min-height:199px\"><img class=\"wp-block-cover__image-background wp-image-616 size-large\" alt=\"\" src=\"http://homemade-circus.local/wp-content/uploads/2023/07/Untitled-design-13-1024x576.png\" style=\"object-position:50% 50%\" data-object-fit=\"cover\" data-object-position=\"50% 50%\"/><span aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"wp-block-cover__background has-background-dim\" style=\"background-color:#f2eaf9\"></span><div class=\"wp-block-cover__inner-container\"><!-- wp:heading -->\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Adapting for Parkinsons:</strong></h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>•<strong> Connect through throwing:</strong> beach balls are safe to bat around. When a classic involuntary movement sends the ball flying off in a random direction, rather than being a problem, this tends to spark energy, laughter and bonding within the group. Try encouraging participants to catch, call a name and make eye contact before throwing.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph --></div></div>\n<!-- /wp:cover -->','Beach Balls','','publish','closed','closed','','beach-balls','','','2026-08-20 12:35:27','2026-08-20 12:35:27','',0,'https://homemadecircus.yme.so/?post_type=activity&#038;p=413',0,'activity','',0),(414,3,'2024-03-11 14:37:05','2024-03-11 14:37:05','','BEACH BALLS - Activity Info Sheet - Homemade Circus','','inherit','open','closed','','beach-balls-activity-info-sheet-homemade-circus','','','2024-03-19 13:42:28','2024-03-19 13:42:28','',413,'https://homemadecircus.yme.so/wp-content/uploads/2024/03/BEACH-BALLS-Activity-Info-Sheet-Homemade-Circus.pdf',0,'attachment','application/pdf',0),(415,3,'2024-03-19 13:35:49','2024-03-19 13:35:49','<!-- wp:paragraph {\"className\":\"wp-embed-aspect-16-9 wp-has-aspect-ratio\"} -->\n<p class=\"wp-embed-aspect-16-9 wp-has-aspect-ratio\">Ribbons are really eye-catching because they are bright and colourful. People love enjoy choosing their favourite colour and creating different shapes and movements. </p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph {\"className\":\"wp-embed-aspect-16-9 wp-has-aspect-ratio\"} -->\n<p class=\"wp-embed-aspect-16-9 wp-has-aspect-ratio\">This is a great activity for groups or partner work and the movements can be easily scaled up or down depending on the mobility levels of those taking part in the workshop.&nbsp;</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph {\"className\":\"wp-embed-aspect-16-9 wp-has-aspect-ratio\"} -->\n<p class=\"wp-embed-aspect-16-9 wp-has-aspect-ratio\">In this video we will demonstrate different movements and shapes you can make, and show you how to adapt the movement to make it easier or more challenging. We’ll show you some of our favourite ribbon games which you can incorporate into your workshop.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:embed {\"url\":\"https://youtu.be/pxDG2O9iLBk\",\"type\":\"video\",\"providerNameSlug\":\"youtube\",\"responsive\":true,\"className\":\"wp-embed-aspect-16-9 wp-has-aspect-ratio\"} -->\n<figure class=\"wp-block-embed is-type-video is-provider-youtube wp-block-embed-youtube wp-embed-aspect-16-9 wp-has-aspect-ratio\"><div class=\"wp-block-embed__wrapper\">\nhttps://youtu.be/pxDG2O9iLBk\n</div></figure>\n<!-- /wp:embed -->','Ribbons','','publish','closed','closed','','ribbons','','','2026-08-20 12:35:48','2026-08-20 12:35:48','',0,'https://homemadecircus.yme.so/?post_type=activity&#038;p=415',0,'activity','',0),(416,3,'2024-03-11 15:01:21','2024-03-11 15:01:21','','RIBBONS - Activity Info Sheet - Homemade Circus','','inherit','open','closed','','ribbons-activity-info-sheet-homemade-circus','','','2024-03-19 13:35:50','2024-03-19 13:35:50','',415,'https://homemadecircus.yme.so/wp-content/uploads/2024/03/RIBBONS-Activity-Info-Sheet-Homemade-Circus.pdf',0,'attachment','application/pdf',0),(417,3,'2024-03-19 13:31:16','2024-03-19 13:31:16','<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>We use the parachute as a gentle and calming activity to bring our circus workshops to an end. People enjoy holding and moving the parachute together, working as a team. The activities we will show you in this video are all about encouraging connection and collaboration. </p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>You can add a beach ball or a juggling ball or two to the parachute to make the activity more challenging and you can vary the movement of the parachute according to the music you are playing. Parachutes are a lot of fun and are a really inclusive way to bring everyone together!</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:embed {\"url\":\"https://youtu.be/zsLkHSmFp0c\",\"type\":\"video\",\"providerNameSlug\":\"youtube\",\"responsive\":true,\"className\":\"wp-embed-aspect-16-9 wp-has-aspect-ratio\"} -->\n<figure class=\"wp-block-embed is-type-video is-provider-youtube wp-block-embed-youtube wp-embed-aspect-16-9 wp-has-aspect-ratio\"><div class=\"wp-block-embed__wrapper\">\nhttps://youtu.be/zsLkHSmFp0c\n</div></figure>\n<!-- /wp:embed -->\n\n<!-- wp:cover {\"url\":\"http://homemade-circus.local/wp-content/uploads/2023/07/Untitled-design-13-1024x576.png\",\"id\":616,\"dimRatio\":50,\"customOverlayColor\":\"#f2eaf9\",\"isUserOverlayColor\":true,\"focalPoint\":{\"x\":0.5,\"y\":0.5},\"minHeight\":220,\"minHeightUnit\":\"px\",\"isDark\":false,\"sizeSlug\":\"large\",\"style\":{\"color\":{\"duotone\":\"unset\"}},\"layout\":{\"type\":\"constrained\"}} -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-cover is-light\" style=\"min-height:220px\"><img class=\"wp-block-cover__image-background wp-image-616 size-large\" alt=\"\" src=\"http://homemade-circus.local/wp-content/uploads/2023/07/Untitled-design-13-1024x576.png\" style=\"object-position:50% 50%\" data-object-fit=\"cover\" data-object-position=\"50% 50%\"/><span aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"wp-block-cover__background has-background-dim\" style=\"background-color:#f2eaf9\"></span><div class=\"wp-block-cover__inner-container\"><!-- wp:heading -->\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Adapting for Parkinsons:</strong></h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>In a group parachute activity, each person\'s individual movement has only a small effect on the parachute as a whole, since it\'s shaped by everyone moving together.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>• <strong>Room for Involuntary Movement</strong>: this means if someone experiences a tremor or freezing moment, it won\'t impact the activity. Everyone can take part with their own capacity of movement and still have a positive experience. </p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph --></div></div>\n<!-- /wp:cover -->','Parachute','','publish','closed','closed','','parachute','','','2026-08-20 12:36:04','2026-08-20 12:36:04','',0,'https://homemadecircus.yme.so/?post_type=activity&#038;p=417',0,'activity','',0),(419,3,'2024-03-11 15:06:27','2024-03-11 15:06:27','','PARACHUTE - Activity Info Sheet - Homemade Circus','','inherit','open','closed','','parachute-activity-info-sheet-homemade-circus','','','2024-03-19 13:32:23','2024-03-19 13:32:23','',417,'https://homemadecircus.yme.so/wp-content/uploads/2024/03/PARACHUTE-Activity-Info-Sheet-Homemade-Circus.pdf',0,'attachment','application/pdf',0),(427,3,'2024-03-19 13:28:49','2024-03-19 13:28:49','','Parachute','','inherit','open','closed','','9','','','2024-03-19 13:29:26','2024-03-19 13:29:26','',417,'https://homemadecircus.yme.so/wp-content/uploads/2024/03/9.png',0,'attachment','image/png',0),(428,3,'2024-03-19 13:33:59','2024-03-19 13:33:59','','ribbons','','inherit','open','closed','','8','','','2024-03-19 13:34:30','2024-03-19 13:34:30','',415,'https://homemadecircus.yme.so/wp-content/uploads/2024/03/8.png',0,'attachment','image/png',0),(430,3,'2024-03-19 13:41:22','2024-03-19 13:41:22','','beach balls','','inherit','open','closed','','11','','','2024-03-19 13:42:23','2024-03-19 13:42:23','',413,'https://homemadecircus.yme.so/wp-content/uploads/2024/03/11.png',0,'attachment','image/png',0),(431,3,'2024-03-19 13:46:14','2024-03-19 13:46:14','','blocks','','inherit','open','closed','','7','','','2024-03-19 13:47:28','2024-03-19 13:47:28','',408,'https://homemadecircus.yme.so/wp-content/uploads/2024/03/7.png',0,'attachment','image/png',0),(432,3,'2024-03-19 13:51:11','2024-03-19 13:51:11','','bunting','','inherit','open','closed','','10','','','2024-03-19 13:56:33','2024-03-19 13:56:33','',411,'https://homemadecircus.yme.so/wp-content/uploads/2024/03/10.png',0,'attachment','image/png',0),(433,3,'2024-03-19 14:25:48','2024-03-19 14:25:48','<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>We\'re so glad you\'re ready to start your circus adventure in care homes with us!  To begin, watch the short video below and our circus artist Charlene will explain how to navigate the toolkit and get the most out of it. </p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:embed {\"url\":\"https://youtu.be/hkc5V3amLzg\",\"type\":\"video\",\"providerNameSlug\":\"youtube\",\"responsive\":true,\"className\":\"wp-embed-aspect-16-9 wp-has-aspect-ratio\"} -->\n<figure class=\"wp-block-embed is-type-video is-provider-youtube wp-block-embed-youtube wp-embed-aspect-16-9 wp-has-aspect-ratio\"><div class=\"wp-block-embed__wrapper\">\nhttps://youtu.be/hkc5V3amLzg\n</div></figure>\n<!-- /wp:embed -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Each activity page includes everything you need to know, like details of where to get the equipment, how long the activity takes and who the activity is suited for. We suggest starting with the \'Coloured Scarves\' activity and working your way down. </p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>When you\'re ready choose an activity from the left-hand menu to get started!</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->','Welcome to the toolkit','','inherit','closed','closed','','42-revision-v1','','','2024-03-19 14:25:48','2024-03-19 14:25:48','',42,'https://homemadecircus.yme.so/?p=433',0,'revision','',0),(434,3,'2024-03-19 14:26:22','2024-03-19 14:26:22','<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>We\'re so glad you\'re ready to start your circus adventure in care homes with us!  To begin, watch the short video below and our circus artist Charlene will explain how to navigate the toolkit and get the most out of it.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Each activity page includes everything you need to know, like details of where to get the equipment, how long the activity takes and who the activity is suited for. We suggest starting with the \'Coloured Scarves\' activity and working your way down. </p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>When you\'re ready choose an activity from the left-hand menu to get started!</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:embed {\"url\":\"https://youtu.be/hkc5V3amLzg\",\"type\":\"video\",\"providerNameSlug\":\"youtube\",\"responsive\":true,\"className\":\"wp-embed-aspect-16-9 wp-has-aspect-ratio\"} -->\n<figure class=\"wp-block-embed is-type-video is-provider-youtube wp-block-embed-youtube wp-embed-aspect-16-9 wp-has-aspect-ratio\"><div class=\"wp-block-embed__wrapper\">\nhttps://youtu.be/hkc5V3amLzg\n</div></figure>\n<!-- /wp:embed -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->','Welcome to the toolkit','','inherit','closed','closed','','42-revision-v1','','','2024-03-19 14:26:22','2024-03-19 14:26:22','',42,'https://homemadecircus.yme.so/?p=434',0,'revision','',0),(435,3,'2024-03-19 14:27:33','2024-03-19 14:27:33','<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>We\'re so glad you\'re ready to start your circus adventure in care homes with us!  To begin, watch the short video below and our circus artist Charlene will explain how to navigate the toolkit and get the most out of it.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Each activity page includes everything you need to know, like details of where to get the equipment, how long the activity takes and who the activity is suited for. We suggest starting with the \'Coloured Scarves\' activity and working your way down. </p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:embed {\"url\":\"https://youtu.be/hkc5V3amLzg\",\"type\":\"video\",\"providerNameSlug\":\"youtube\",\"responsive\":true,\"className\":\"wp-embed-aspect-16-9 wp-has-aspect-ratio\"} -->\n<figure class=\"wp-block-embed is-type-video is-provider-youtube wp-block-embed-youtube wp-embed-aspect-16-9 wp-has-aspect-ratio\"><div class=\"wp-block-embed__wrapper\">\nhttps://youtu.be/hkc5V3amLzg\n</div></figure>\n<!-- /wp:embed -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p><strong>When you\'re ready choose an activity from the left-hand menu to get started!</strong></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->','Welcome to the toolkit','','inherit','closed','closed','','42-revision-v1','','','2024-03-19 14:27:33','2024-03-19 14:27:33','',42,'https://homemadecircus.yme.so/?p=435',0,'revision','',0),(436,3,'2024-03-19 14:31:26','2024-03-19 14:31:26','<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>We\'re so glad you\'re ready to start your circus adventure in care homes with us!  To begin, watch the short video below and our circus artist Charlene will explain how to navigate the toolkit and get the most out of it.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Each activity page includes everything you need to know, like details of where to get the equipment, how long the activity takes and who the activity is suited for. We suggest starting with the \'Coloured Scarves\' activity and working your way down. </p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:embed {\"url\":\"https://youtu.be/hkc5V3amLzg\",\"type\":\"video\",\"providerNameSlug\":\"youtube\",\"responsive\":true,\"className\":\"wp-embed-aspect-16-9 wp-has-aspect-ratio\"} -->\n<figure class=\"wp-block-embed is-type-video is-provider-youtube wp-block-embed-youtube wp-embed-aspect-16-9 wp-has-aspect-ratio\"><div class=\"wp-block-embed__wrapper\">\nhttps://youtu.be/hkc5V3amLzg\n</div></figure>\n<!-- /wp:embed -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p><strong>When you\'re ready, choose an activity from the left-hand menu to get started!</strong></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->','Welcome to the toolkit','','inherit','closed','closed','','42-revision-v1','','','2024-03-19 14:31:26','2024-03-19 14:31:26','',42,'https://homemadecircus.yme.so/?p=436',0,'revision','',0),(443,3,'2024-03-19 14:43:12','2024-03-19 14:43:12','','Sample Workshop Plan - Homemade Circus','','inherit','open','closed','','sample-workshop-plan-homemade-circus','','','2024-03-19 14:43:12','2024-03-19 14:43:12','',0,'https://homemadecircus.yme.so/wp-content/uploads/2024/03/Sample-Workshop-Plan-Homemade-Circus.pdf',0,'attachment','application/pdf',0),(444,3,'2024-03-19 14:43:21','2024-03-19 14:43:21','','Workshop Checklist - Homemade Circus','','inherit','open','closed','','workshop-checklist-homemade-circus','','','2024-03-19 14:43:21','2024-03-19 14:43:21','',0,'https://homemadecircus.yme.so/wp-content/uploads/2024/03/Workshop-Checklist-Homemade-Circus.pdf',0,'attachment','application/pdf',0),(448,3,'2024-03-19 15:13:47','2024-03-19 15:13:47','','20230313-7R405421','','inherit','open','closed','','20230313-7r405421','','','2024-03-19 15:14:58','2024-03-19 15:14:58','',306,'https://homemadecircus.yme.so/wp-content/uploads/2024/03/20230313-7R405421.jpg',0,'attachment','image/jpeg',0),(449,3,'2024-03-19 15:23:17','2024-03-19 15:23:17','','asd','','inherit','open','closed','','asd','','','2024-03-19 15:23:17','2024-03-19 15:23:17','',306,'https://homemadecircus.yme.so/wp-content/uploads/2024/03/asd.jpg',0,'attachment','image/jpeg',0),(450,3,'2024-03-19 15:27:29','2024-03-19 15:27:29','<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>As always, health and safety is an important consideration, especially when using new equipment. Some exercises involve touch and we always want to make sure everyone we’re working with feels completely comfortable with all parts of the activity. Follow these steps to make sure you have all the necessary Health and Safety in place before your session:</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:image {\"id\":449,\"sizeSlug\":\"large\",\"linkDestination\":\"none\"} -->\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large\"><img src=\"https://homemadecircus.yme.so/wp-content/uploads/2024/03/asd-1024x521.jpg\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-449\"/></figure>\n<!-- /wp:image -->\n\n<!-- wp:spacer {\"height\":\"24px\"} -->\n<div style=\"height:24px\" aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"wp-block-spacer\"></div>\n<!-- /wp:spacer -->\n\n<!-- wp:list -->\n<ul><!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>Make sure you <strong>fill out a risk assessment form</strong> before your workshop. You can use our template which can be found in the \'Useful Links\' section on the right-hand side of this page.<br></li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>Be sure that you have enough care home staff in the room at all times. <strong>Ideally you need 2-3 care home staff working alongside you</strong> to support you in delivering the session. Brief them on the activities, structure and Health and Safety considerations beforehand.<br></li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>Check that each participant or resident has <strong>enough space to stretch their arms and legs</strong> without clashing.<br></li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><strong>Leave space for people to exit and enter the workshop circle</strong> without disturbing the rest of the participants.<br></li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>If using touch in your session, let the person know what you are planning to do and <strong>ask permission before you touch them</strong>. For example, when using a Flower Stick to massage each others\' hands and arms, you can say \'If you want, we can try using the sticks to gently massage your arms and hands, would you be okay with that?\'. <br></li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>If you’re assisting someone in moving a part of their body you can also <strong>check with them that it feels ok and nothing is painful</strong>.<br></li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>Ensure you <strong>always do a light warm-up and cool-down</strong> before and after every sessions so that no one gets hurt.<br></li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item --></ul>\n<!-- /wp:list -->','Health and Safety','','inherit','closed','closed','','306-revision-v1','','','2024-03-19 15:27:29','2024-03-19 15:27:29','',306,'https://homemadecircus.yme.so/?p=450',0,'revision','',0),(452,3,'2024-03-19 15:42:12','2024-03-19 15:42:12','','hgf','','inherit','open','closed','','hgf','','','2024-03-19 15:42:12','2024-03-19 15:42:12','',310,'https://homemadecircus.yme.so/wp-content/uploads/2024/03/hgf.jpg',0,'attachment','image/jpeg',0),(453,3,'2024-03-19 15:46:21','2024-03-19 15:46:21','','20230313-7R405039-Edit (2)','','inherit','open','closed','','20230313-7r405039-edit-2','','','2024-03-19 15:46:50','2024-03-19 15:46:50','',310,'https://homemadecircus.yme.so/wp-content/uploads/2024/03/20230313-7R405039-Edit-2.jpg',0,'attachment','image/jpeg',0),(454,3,'2024-03-19 15:48:32','2024-03-19 15:48:32','<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p><strong>Being organised and prepared before facilitating your workshop will help it run smoothly. Use the \'Workshop Checklist\' provided under \'Useful Links\' to confirm you have all necessary materials to start. </strong></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>That being said, the playful essence of these workshops means surprises can occur. Stay flexible, improvise when needed and most importantly, have fun - the more you run these sessions, the more comfortable you\'ll become handling unexpected developments.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading -->\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Music:</strong></h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:image {\"id\":452,\"sizeSlug\":\"large\",\"linkDestination\":\"none\"} -->\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large\"><img src=\"https://homemadecircus.yme.so/wp-content/uploads/2024/03/hgf-1024x473.jpg\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-452\"/></figure>\n<!-- /wp:image -->\n\n<!-- wp:spacer {\"height\":\"30px\"} -->\n<div style=\"height:30px\" aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"wp-block-spacer\"></div>\n<!-- /wp:spacer -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Circus activities work well when there is music playing. It helps loosen everyone up and direct the energy of the room. Head to our Spotify page to check out the playlists we\'ve set up to suit various moods. You can find the link under \'Useful Links\' in the right-hand side of this page. Consider:</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:list -->\n<ul><!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><strong>Is the volume suitable</strong> for the group?</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>We recommend <strong>using music without words</strong> (instrumental) during activities when giving instructions. This is crucial for <strong>helping people to focus on what you\'re saying</strong></li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>What type of music are you playing to <strong>set the mood</strong>? We like to choose tracks which are bright and uplifting</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><strong>Music is a powerful way of connecting with people who are living with dementia</strong>. We’ve witnessed some amazing reactions when people hear their favourite song. <strong>Spend some time finding out what kind of music your participants are interested in</strong>. You could then curate a playlist for the participants based on their own musical tastes or favourite songs - which <strong>really helps with engagement and community-building.</strong></li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>Sometimes it may be hard find this out from the participants so <strong>remember to ask your colleagues</strong> as they may have more knowledge about an individual’s needs, likes and dislikes</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item --></ul>\n<!-- /wp:list -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading -->\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Setting up the room:</strong></h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:image {\"id\":453,\"sizeSlug\":\"large\",\"linkDestination\":\"none\"} -->\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large\"><img src=\"https://homemadecircus.yme.so/wp-content/uploads/2024/03/20230313-7R405039-Edit-2-1024x403.jpg\" alt=\"A group of older people and care home staff sit in a circle and run bunting between them, smiling\" class=\"wp-image-453\"/></figure>\n<!-- /wp:image -->\n\n<!-- wp:spacer {\"height\":\"28px\"} -->\n<div style=\"height:28px\" aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"wp-block-spacer\"></div>\n<!-- /wp:spacer -->\n\n<!-- wp:list -->\n<ul><!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><strong>Choose a large, well-lit comfortable room</strong> where you will not be interrupted, and <strong>set up the chairs in a large circle with space between each chair</strong>. This is important so that participants have room to extend their arms and use the equipment without bumping into one another. <strong>Make sure there is an open space at the centre of the circle for you to stand</strong> when delivering instructions and for the participants to see everyone else across the circle</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>Ensure there are <strong>chairs set up in the circle for colleagues, assistants or visitors</strong> so that everyone is included</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><strong>Switch off any TV or radio</strong> </li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><strong>Start your music just before the session</strong> to set the mood</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><strong>Introduce yourself</strong> and the other people who are leading the workshop. You might want to ask everyone in the circle to say their name and others to respond by giving them a verbal hello or smile or a wave back</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><strong>Start the workshop with some introductory games</strong>, to connect with the participants whilst the other participants are arriving. Once everyone is in the room commence with an essential physical warm up to ensure safe delivery</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item --></ul>\n<!-- /wp:list -->','Before your Workshop','','inherit','closed','closed','','310-revision-v1','','','2024-03-19 15:48:32','2024-03-19 15:48:32','',310,'https://homemadecircus.yme.so/?p=454',0,'revision','',0),(456,3,'2024-03-19 15:54:37','2024-03-19 15:54:37','','20240206-SA902108','','inherit','open','closed','','20240206-sa902108','','','2024-03-19 15:55:01','2024-03-19 15:55:01','',314,'https://homemadecircus.yme.so/wp-content/uploads/2024/03/20240206-SA902108.jpg',0,'attachment','image/jpeg',0),(457,3,'2024-03-19 15:56:52','2024-03-19 15:56:52','<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>The top priority when running your workshop is not perfecting skills, but creating a safe, judgement-free space for participants to try new things, play around, and mess up. With experimentation comes inevitable mistakes - it is key to encourage an environment where people feel comfortable being imperfect and having fun. Try putting participants at ease with these strategies:</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading -->\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Making your workshop a welcoming space</strong>:</h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:image {\"id\":456,\"sizeSlug\":\"large\",\"linkDestination\":\"none\"} -->\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large\"><img src=\"https://homemadecircus.yme.so/wp-content/uploads/2024/03/20240206-SA902108-1024x488.jpg\" alt=\"A care home staff member helps an older person to walk across the room by holding her hands\" class=\"wp-image-456\"/></figure>\n<!-- /wp:image -->\n\n<!-- wp:spacer {\"height\":\"19px\"} -->\n<div style=\"height:19px\" aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"wp-block-spacer\"></div>\n<!-- /wp:spacer -->\n\n<!-- wp:list -->\n<ul><!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><strong>Greet Everyone and Introduce Yourself -</strong> Making sure you give each participant a <strong>warm personal welcome </strong>as they enter the room, introducing yourself and being clear to them about what they are about to do in the session – although small, this interaction helps encourage participants to be more likely to listen and be attentive. When possible try to use people’s names when you are addressing them.</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><strong>Make eye contact</strong>  - ensuring that you are making direct, gentle eye contact to everyone so that they understand that you are making time for them. Always use eye contact when you are working with someone on a one-to-one basis. Observe their body language and adapt the exercise if required to ensure that participants always feel comfortable</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><strong>Take your time</strong> - don’t rush the activity and go with the flow of the group. Always remember to take your time, allow for pauses so the participants can process what you\'re saying. Ensure that you demonstrate the activities clearly</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><strong>Gently get the group attention </strong>- it can get very noisy during workshops, especially when people are having a lot of fun and conversation. Try <strong>not to yell above people </strong>as this can be distressing for some. Use methods such as select gestures like waving your arms in the air and slowly one by one others will copy or stop what their doing to give your their attention. Other method include tapping / clapping a rhythm repeatedly for others to join or even singing a song</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><strong>Make it clear who’s leading and who’s supporting </strong>- there should always be one person leading the activity and others supporting. If a support-person switches to a leader role during the session - this should be clearly communicated and shown to the participants, so that they know where the instructions are coming from</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><strong>Encourage, encourage, encourage  -</strong> At first, residents can sometimes be confused and a bit resistant to the activities. Make sure to calmly and positively reassure them, allow them to take it slow, encourage them to make mistakes and remind them that they don’t have to do it perfectly. </li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><strong>Managing other staff / helpers</strong> – As the session leader, it’s important to communicate clearly to support staff what the session plan is, how they can best support what needs to be achieved in each exercise. Your colleagues working with you in the room are your allies, use them to help you get the attention/focus of the participants so that your directions and instructions are clearly received.</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><strong>Lead with care and confidence </strong>- ensure you can be seen by everyone, try not to cover your face or mouth, speak clearly, at a steady pace and loud enough for everyone to hear. Make eye contact and repetition with a physical demonstration always helps. If you are working with seated participants you may want to consider kneeling or sitting so that you are on the same level as them</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><strong>Read the room -</strong> When working with the group, always remember to be patient and read the energy of the room. If everyone is quieter than usual play a gentle music track accompanied by a calmer activity before building up to something more energetic</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item --></ul>\n<!-- /wp:list -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading -->\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Introducing movement:</strong></h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:list -->\n<ul><!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>Encourage the group to follow or copy your movement - start with <strong>gentle dynamic stretches or gestures </strong>of the arms - nothing static to keep the muscles moving and encourage blood flow to warm the body up</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item --></ul>\n<!-- /wp:list -->\n\n<!-- wp:list -->\n<ul><!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>Low impact dancing to music - <strong>teach the group a few movements that directly resonate to the lyrics of the music</strong> (e.g. when the song say’s up - you wave your hands up) then let them freestyle inbetween the movements or get the group to teach you some of their movements to add to the song</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item --></ul>\n<!-- /wp:list -->\n\n<!-- wp:list -->\n<ul><!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>Working on <strong>dexterity</strong> - playing the piano gestures on their legs, in the air etc. opening and closing the hands and stretching the fingers to strengthen and awaken the muscles</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item --></ul>\n<!-- /wp:list -->\n\n<!-- wp:list -->\n<ul><!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>Making connections - <strong>suggest to residents to greet and meet each other </strong>across the room, or next to each other by waving or sending saying hello assisted -then maybe get them to make a physical connection like a hand shake or passing an item to one another (e.g. beach ball)</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item --></ul>\n<!-- /wp:list -->\n\n<!-- wp:list -->\n<ul><!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><strong>Checking in</strong> regularly with everyone to make sure that they’re comfortable, they understand what’s happening and ready to take on the next activity</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item --></ul>\n<!-- /wp:list -->','During your Workshop','','inherit','closed','closed','','314-revision-v1','','','2024-03-19 15:56:52','2024-03-19 15:56:52','',314,'https://homemadecircus.yme.so/?p=457',0,'revision','',0),(459,3,'2024-03-19 16:51:20','2024-03-19 16:51:20','','20240206-SA901769','','inherit','open','closed','','20240206-sa901769','','','2024-03-19 16:51:20','2024-03-19 16:51:20','',314,'https://homemadecircus.yme.so/wp-content/uploads/2024/03/20240206-SA901769.jpg',0,'attachment','image/jpeg',0),(460,3,'2024-03-19 17:00:33','2024-03-19 17:00:33','<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>The top priority when running your workshop is not perfecting skills, but creating a safe, judgement-free space for participants to try new things, play around, and mess up. With experimentation comes inevitable mistakes - it is key to encourage an environment where people feel comfortable being imperfect and having fun. Try putting participants at ease with these strategies:</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading -->\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Making your workshop a welcoming space</strong>:</h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:image {\"id\":456,\"sizeSlug\":\"large\",\"linkDestination\":\"none\"} -->\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large\"><img src=\"https://homemadecircus.yme.so/wp-content/uploads/2024/03/20240206-SA902108-1024x488.jpg\" alt=\"A care home staff member helps an older person to walk across the room by holding her hands\" class=\"wp-image-456\"/></figure>\n<!-- /wp:image -->\n\n<!-- wp:spacer {\"height\":\"19px\"} -->\n<div style=\"height:19px\" aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"wp-block-spacer\"></div>\n<!-- /wp:spacer -->\n\n<!-- wp:list -->\n<ul><!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><strong>Greet Everyone and Introduce Yourself -</strong> Making sure you give each participant a <strong>warm personal welcome </strong>as they enter the room, introducing yourself and being clear about what you will do together  in the session – although small, this interaction helps encourage participants to be more likely to listen and be attentive. When possible try to use people’s names when you are addressing them.</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><strong>Make eye contact</strong>  - ensuring that you are making direct, gentle eye contact to everyone so that they understand that you are making time for them. Always use eye contact when you are working with someone on a one-to-one basis. Observe their body language and adapt the exercise if required to ensure that participants always feel comfortable</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><strong>Take your time</strong> - don’t rush the activity and go with the flow of the group. Always remember to take your time, allow for pauses so the participants can process what you\'re saying. Ensure that you demonstrate the activities clearly</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><strong>Gently get the group attention </strong>- it can get very noisy during workshops, especially when people are having a lot of fun and conversation. <strong>Try not to yell above people </strong>as this can be distressing for some. Use methods such as select gestures like waving your arms in the air and slowly one by one others will copy or stop what their doing to give your their attention. Other method include tapping / clapping a rhythm repeatedly for others to join or even singing a song</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><strong>Make it clear who’s leading and who’s supporting </strong>- there should always be one person leading the activity and others supporting. If a support-person switches to a leader role during the session - this should be clearly communicated and shown to the participants, so that they know where the instructions are coming from</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><strong>Encourage, encourage, encourage  -</strong> At first, residents can sometimes be confused and a bit resistant to the activities. Make sure to calmly and positively reassure them, allow them to take it slow, encourage them to make mistakes and remind them that they don’t have to do it perfectly. </li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><strong>Managing other staff / helpers</strong> – As the session leader, it’s important to communicate clearly to support staff what the session plan is, how they can best support what needs to be achieved in each exercise. Your colleagues working with you in the room are your allies, use them to help you get the attention/focus of the participants so that your directions and instructions are clearly received.</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><strong>Lead with care and confidence </strong>- ensure you can be seen by everyone, try not to cover your face or mouth, speak clearly, at a steady pace and loud enough for everyone to hear. Make eye contact and repetition with a physical demonstration always helps. If you are working with seated participants you may want to consider kneeling or sitting so that you are on the same level as them</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><strong>Read the room -</strong> When working with the group, always remember to be patient and read the energy of the room. If everyone is quieter than usual play a gentle music track accompanied by a calmer activity before building up to something more energetic</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item --></ul>\n<!-- /wp:list -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading -->\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Introducing movement:</strong></h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:image {\"id\":459,\"sizeSlug\":\"large\",\"linkDestination\":\"none\"} -->\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large\"><img src=\"https://homemadecircus.yme.so/wp-content/uploads/2024/03/20240206-SA901769-1024x445.jpg\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-459\"/></figure>\n<!-- /wp:image -->\n\n<!-- wp:list -->\n<ul><!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>Encourage the group to follow or copy your movement - start with <strong>gentle dynamic stretches or gestures </strong>of the arms - nothing static to keep the muscles moving and encourage blood flow to warm the body up</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>Low impact dancing to music - <strong>teach the group a few movements that directly resonate to the lyrics of the music</strong> (e.g. when the song say’s up - you wave your hands up) then let them freestyle inbetween the movements or get the group to teach you some of their movements to add to the song</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>Working on <strong>dexterity</strong> - playing the piano gestures on their legs, in the air etc. opening and closing the hands and stretching the fingers to strengthen and awaken the muscles</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>Making connections - <strong>suggest to residents to greet and meet each other </strong>across the room, or next to each other by waving or sending saying hello assisted -then maybe get them to make a physical connection like a hand shake or passing an item to one another (e.g. beach ball)</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><strong>Checking in</strong> regularly with everyone to make sure that they’re comfortable, they understand what’s happening and ready to take on the next activity</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item --></ul>\n<!-- /wp:list -->','During your Workshop','','inherit','closed','closed','','314-revision-v1','','','2024-03-19 17:00:33','2024-03-19 17:00:33','',314,'https://homemadecircus.yme.so/?p=460',0,'revision','',0),(462,3,'2024-03-19 17:07:11','2024-03-19 17:07:11','','20240206-SA901584','','inherit','open','closed','','20240206-sa901584','','','2024-03-19 17:07:34','2024-03-19 17:07:34','',317,'https://homemadecircus.yme.so/wp-content/uploads/2024/03/20240206-SA901584.jpg',0,'attachment','image/jpeg',0),(463,3,'2024-03-19 17:12:11','2024-03-19 17:12:11','<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>It is nice to round-off the activities after you are finished so that everyone is left feeling content and the connected feeling continues. It is also a great time to take notes for yourself of what did and didn\'t work, so that you can focus on those in the next session. Here are some ideas of ways to close the session that will leave participants excited for the next one, choose what feels right for the room:</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading -->\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Closing the session:</strong></h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:image {\"id\":462,\"sizeSlug\":\"large\",\"linkDestination\":\"none\"} -->\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large\"><img src=\"https://homemadecircus.yme.so/wp-content/uploads/2024/03/20240206-SA901584-1024x486.jpg\" alt=\"a circus workshop leader shakes hands with an older workshop participant\" class=\"wp-image-462\"/></figure>\n<!-- /wp:image -->\n\n<!-- wp:spacer {\"height\":\"25px\"} -->\n<div style=\"height:25px\" aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"wp-block-spacer\"></div>\n<!-- /wp:spacer -->\n\n<!-- wp:list -->\n<ul><!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><strong>Cooldown</strong> and light movement/stretching</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>If the atmosphere seems lively, you can keep the music playing and <strong>use this as socialising time</strong></li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><strong>Serving tea &amp; cake</strong> whilst everyone’s together</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><strong>Remind people when the next session is</strong> while they’re in the room</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>If you’re keeping <strong>records of people’s attendance and any surprising interactions you noticed</strong>, it’s a great time to immediately write this up straight after while you remember</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>We’d love to hear about your experience so <strong>it’s also a good time to send us any feedback at <a href=\"mailto:info@upswing.org.uk\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">info@upswing.org.uk</a></strong>, we would appreciate any thoughts you had about the Digital toolkit, it\'s content or how your sessions are going</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item --></ul>\n<!-- /wp:list -->','After your Workshop','','inherit','closed','closed','','317-revision-v1','','','2024-03-19 17:12:11','2024-03-19 17:12:11','',317,'https://homemadecircus.yme.so/?p=463',0,'revision','',0),(465,3,'2024-03-19 17:14:21','2024-03-19 17:14:21','<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>The top priority when running your workshop is not perfecting skills, but creating a safe, judgement-free space for participants to try new things, play around, and mess up. With experimentation comes inevitable mistakes - it is key to encourage an environment where people feel comfortable being imperfect and having fun. Try putting participants at ease with these strategies:</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading -->\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Making your workshop a welcoming space</strong>:</h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:image {\"id\":456,\"sizeSlug\":\"large\",\"linkDestination\":\"none\"} -->\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large\"><img src=\"https://homemadecircus.yme.so/wp-content/uploads/2024/03/20240206-SA902108-1024x488.jpg\" alt=\"A care home staff member helps an older person to walk across the room by holding her hands\" class=\"wp-image-456\"/></figure>\n<!-- /wp:image -->\n\n<!-- wp:spacer {\"height\":\"19px\"} -->\n<div style=\"height:19px\" aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"wp-block-spacer\"></div>\n<!-- /wp:spacer -->\n\n<!-- wp:list -->\n<ul><!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><strong>Greet Everyone and Introduce Yourself -</strong> Making sure you give each participant a <strong>warm personal welcome </strong>as they enter the room, introducing yourself and being clear about what you will do together  in the session – although small, this interaction helps encourage participants to be more likely to listen and be attentive. When possible try to use people’s names when you are addressing them.</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><strong>Make eye contact</strong>&nbsp; - ensuring that you are making direct, gentle eye contact to everyone so that they understand that you are making time for them. Always use eye contact when you are working with someone on a one-to-one basis. Observe their body language and adapt the exercise if required to ensure that participants always feel comfortable</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><strong>Take your time</strong> - don’t rush the activity and go with the flow of the group. Always remember to take your time, allow for pauses so the participants can process what you\'re saying. Ensure that you demonstrate the activities clearly</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><strong>Gently get the group attention </strong>- it can get very noisy during workshops, especially when people are having a lot of fun and conversation. <strong>Try not to yell above people </strong>as this can be distressing for some. Use methods such as select gestures like waving your arms in the air and slowly one by one others will copy or stop what their doing to give your their attention. Other method include tapping / clapping a rhythm repeatedly for others to join or even singing a song</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><strong>Make it clear who’s leading and who’s supporting </strong>- there should always be one person leading the activity and others supporting. If a support-person switches to a leader role during the session - this should be clearly communicated and shown to the participants, so that they know where the instructions are coming from</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><strong>Encourage, encourage, encourage&nbsp; -</strong> At first, residents can sometimes be confused and a bit resistant to the activities. Make sure to calmly and positively reassure them, allow them to take it slow, encourage them to make mistakes and remind them that they don’t have to do it perfectly. </li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><strong>Managing other staff / helpers</strong> – As the session leader, it’s important to communicate clearly to support staff what the session plan is, how they can best support what needs to be achieved in each exercise. Your colleagues working with you in the room are your allies, use them to help you get the attention/focus of the participants so that your directions and instructions are clearly received.</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><strong>Lead with care and confidence </strong>- ensure you can be seen by everyone, try not to cover your face or mouth, speak clearly, at a steady pace and loud enough for everyone to hear. Make eye contact and repetition with a physical demonstration always helps. If you are working with seated participants you may want to consider kneeling or sitting so that you are on the same level as them</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><strong>Read the room -</strong> When working with the group, always remember to be patient and read the energy of the room. If everyone is quieter than usual play a gentle music track accompanied by a calmer activity before building up to something more energetic</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item --></ul>\n<!-- /wp:list -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading -->\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Introducing movement:</strong></h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:image {\"id\":459,\"sizeSlug\":\"large\",\"linkDestination\":\"none\"} -->\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large\"><img src=\"https://homemadecircus.yme.so/wp-content/uploads/2024/03/20240206-SA901769-1024x445.jpg\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-459\"/></figure>\n<!-- /wp:image -->\n\n<!-- wp:spacer {\"height\":\"25px\"} -->\n<div style=\"height:25px\" aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"wp-block-spacer\"></div>\n<!-- /wp:spacer -->\n\n<!-- wp:list -->\n<ul><!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>Encourage the group to follow or copy your movement - start with <strong>gentle dynamic stretches or gestures </strong>of the arms - nothing static to keep the muscles moving and encourage blood flow to warm the body up</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>Low impact dancing to music - <strong>teach the group a few movements that directly resonate to the lyrics of the music</strong> (e.g. when the song say’s up - you wave your hands up) then let them freestyle inbetween the movements or get the group to teach you some of their movements to add to the song</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>Working on <strong>dexterity</strong> - playing the piano gestures on their legs, in the air etc. opening and closing the hands and stretching the fingers to strengthen and awaken the muscles</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>Making connections - <strong>suggest to residents to greet and meet each other </strong>across the room, or next to each other by waving or sending saying hello assisted -then maybe get them to make a physical connection like a hand shake or passing an item to one another (e.g. beach ball)</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><strong>Checking in</strong> regularly with everyone to make sure that they’re comfortable, they understand what’s happening and ready to take on the next activity</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item --></ul>\n<!-- /wp:list -->','During your Workshop','','inherit','closed','closed','','314-revision-v1','','','2024-03-19 17:14:21','2024-03-19 17:14:21','',314,'https://homemadecircus.yme.so/?p=465',0,'revision','',0),(466,1,'2024-03-20 13:26:22','2024-03-20 13:26:22','{\"fields\":{\"1\":{\"id\":\"1\",\"type\":\"text\",\"label\":\"Name\",\"description\":\"\",\"size\":\"medium\",\"placeholder\":\"\",\"limit_count\":\"1\",\"limit_mode\":\"characters\",\"default_value\":\"\",\"input_mask\":\"\",\"css\":\"\"},\"4\":{\"id\":\"4\",\"type\":\"email\",\"label\":\"Email\",\"description\":\"\",\"required\":\"1\",\"size\":\"medium\",\"placeholder\":\"\",\"confirmation_placeholder\":\"\",\"default_value\":false,\"filter_type\":\"\",\"allowlist\":\"\",\"denylist\":\"\",\"css\":\"\"},\"2\":{\"id\":\"2\",\"type\":\"textarea\",\"label\":\"Message\",\"description\":\"\",\"size\":\"medium\",\"placeholder\":\"\",\"limit_count\":\"1\",\"limit_mode\":\"characters\",\"default_value\":\"\",\"css\":\"\"}},\"id\":\"239\",\"field_id\":5,\"settings\":{\"form_title\":\"Contact Form\",\"form_desc\":\"\",\"submit_text\":\"Submit\",\"submit_text_processing\":\"Sending...\",\"form_class\":\"\",\"submit_class\":\"\",\"ajax_submit\":\"1\",\"notification_enable\":\"1\",\"notifications\":{\"1\":{\"email\":\"{admin_email}\",\"subject\":\"New Message From Homemade Circus Website\",\"sender_name\":\"Homemade Circus\",\"sender_address\":\"info@homemadecircus.yme.so\",\"replyto\":\"\",\"message\":\"{all_fields}\"}},\"confirmations\":{\"1\":{\"type\":\"message\",\"message\":\"<p>Thanks for contacting us! We will be in touch with you shortly.<\\/p>\",\"message_scroll\":\"1\",\"page\":\"54\",\"redirect\":\"\"}},\"antispam\":\"1\",\"anti_spam\":{\"time_limit\":{\"duration\":\"3\"}},\"recaptcha\":\"1\",\"form_tags\":[]},\"meta\":{\"template\":\"blank\"}}','Contact Form','','inherit','closed','closed','','239-revision-v1','','','2024-03-20 13:26:22','2024-03-20 13:26:22','',239,'https://homemadecircus.yme.so/?p=466',0,'revision','',0),(469,1,'2024-04-02 15:46:04','2024-04-02 15:46:04','','Activities','','publish','closed','closed','','activities','','','2024-04-02 15:46:05','2024-04-02 15:46:05','',0,'https://homemadecircus.yme.so/?page_id=469',0,'page','',0),(470,1,'2024-04-02 15:46:04','2024-04-02 15:46:04','','Activities','','inherit','closed','closed','','469-revision-v1','','','2024-04-02 15:46:04','2024-04-02 15:46:04','',469,'https://homemadecircus.yme.so/?p=470',0,'revision','',0),(474,3,'2024-04-25 14:08:51','2024-04-25 14:08:51','','Risk assesment template','','inherit','open','closed','','risk-assesment-template','','','2024-04-25 14:08:51','2024-04-25 14:08:51','',0,'https://homemadecircus.yme.so/wp-content/uploads/2024/04/Risk-assesment-template.pdf',0,'attachment','application/pdf',0),(476,3,'2024-04-25 14:13:03','2024-04-25 14:13:03','<!-- wp:spacer {\"height\":\"17px\"} -->\n<div style=\"height:17px\" aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"wp-block-spacer\"></div>\n<!-- /wp:spacer -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>If you\'ve watched all of the activity videos you might be wondering how to piece these together into your own workshop.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Use the links below to take you through the steps of planning and preparing for your session. We\'ve included everything you should consider before your workshop, including template plans, workshop check lists, playlists and more. If you\'re about to run your first session, print off what you need and take it with you, so that you can refer to it easily during the workshop. </p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Don\'t forget that each activity page also includes an activity reminder/info sheet with bullet points to follow. If you\'d like a reminder during your first few sessions you can print these as well as take them with you.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:spacer {\"height\":\"35px\"} -->\n<div style=\"height:35px\" aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"wp-block-spacer\"></div>\n<!-- /wp:spacer -->\n\n<!-- wp:columns -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-columns\"><!-- wp:column -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-column\"><!-- wp:image {\"id\":272,\"width\":\"384px\",\"height\":\"auto\",\"sizeSlug\":\"full\",\"linkDestination\":\"custom\"} -->\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-full is-resized\"><a href=\"https://homemadecircus.yme.so/health-and-safety/\"><img src=\"https://homemadecircus.yme.so/wp-content/uploads/2023/10/HEALTH-SAFETY-5.png\" alt=\"Health and Safety\" class=\"wp-image-272\" style=\"width:384px;height:auto\"/></a></figure>\n<!-- /wp:image -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph {\"align\":\"left\"} -->\n<p class=\"has-text-align-left\"><a href=\"https://homemadecircus.yme.so/planning-your-workshop/health-and-safety/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Health &amp; Safety</a></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph --></div>\n<!-- /wp:column -->\n\n<!-- wp:column -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-column\"><!-- wp:image {\"id\":274,\"width\":\"368px\",\"height\":\"auto\",\"sizeSlug\":\"full\",\"linkDestination\":\"custom\"} -->\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-full is-resized\"><a href=\"https://homemadecircus.yme.so/before-your-workshop/\"><img src=\"https://homemadecircus.yme.so/wp-content/uploads/2023/10/HEALTH-SAFETY-6.png\" alt=\"Before your workshop\" class=\"wp-image-274\" style=\"width:368px;height:auto\"/></a></figure>\n<!-- /wp:image -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph {\"align\":\"left\"} -->\n<p class=\"has-text-align-left\"><a href=\"https://homemadecircus.yme.so/planning-your-workshop/before-your-workshop/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Before Your Workshop</a></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph --></div>\n<!-- /wp:column --></div>\n<!-- /wp:columns -->\n\n<!-- wp:spacer {\"height\":\"14px\"} -->\n<div style=\"height:14px\" aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"wp-block-spacer\"></div>\n<!-- /wp:spacer -->\n\n<!-- wp:columns -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-columns\"><!-- wp:column -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-column\"><!-- wp:image {\"id\":277,\"width\":\"389px\",\"height\":\"auto\",\"sizeSlug\":\"full\",\"linkDestination\":\"custom\"} -->\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-full is-resized\"><a href=\"https://homemadecircus.yme.so/during-your-workshop/\"><img src=\"https://homemadecircus.yme.so/wp-content/uploads/2023/10/HEALTH-SAFETY-9.png\" alt=\"During your workshop\" class=\"wp-image-277\" style=\"width:389px;height:auto\"/></a></figure>\n<!-- /wp:image -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph {\"align\":\"left\"} -->\n<p class=\"has-text-align-left\"><a href=\"https://homemadecircus.yme.so/planning-your-workshop/during-your-workshop/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">During Your Workshop</a></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph --></div>\n<!-- /wp:column -->\n\n<!-- wp:column -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-column\"><!-- wp:image {\"id\":293,\"width\":\"383px\",\"height\":\"auto\",\"sizeSlug\":\"full\",\"linkDestination\":\"custom\"} -->\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-full is-resized\"><a href=\"https://homemadecircus.yme.so/after-your-workshop/\"><img src=\"https://homemadecircus.yme.so/wp-content/uploads/2023/10/HEALTH-SAFETY-11.png\" alt=\"After your workshop\" class=\"wp-image-293\" style=\"width:383px;height:auto\"/></a></figure>\n<!-- /wp:image -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph {\"align\":\"left\"} -->\n<p class=\"has-text-align-left\"><a href=\"https://homemadecircus.yme.so/planning-your-workshop/after-your-workshop/\">After Your Workshop</a></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph --></div>\n<!-- /wp:column --></div>\n<!-- /wp:columns -->','Planning Your Workshop','','inherit','closed','closed','','258-revision-v1','','','2024-04-25 14:13:03','2024-04-25 14:13:03','',258,'https://homemadecircus.yme.so/?p=476',0,'revision','',0),(484,3,'2024-04-25 17:08:44','2024-04-25 17:08:44','','20230313-7R404981-Edit','','inherit','open','closed','','20230313-7r404981-edit-2','','','2024-04-25 17:08:44','2024-04-25 17:08:44','',44,'https://homemadecircus.yme.so/wp-content/uploads/2024/04/20230313-7R404981-Edit-1.jpg',0,'attachment','image/jpeg',0),(488,3,'2024-04-25 17:11:24','2024-04-25 17:11:24','<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Click the \'+\' symbol next to any questions you\'d like the answer to. If you have any questions that are not answered below, you can email us at <a href=\"mailto:info@upswing.org.uk\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">info@upswing.org.uk</a></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:spacer {\"height\":\"11px\"} -->\n<div style=\"height:11px\" aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"wp-block-spacer\"></div>\n<!-- /wp:spacer -->\n\n<!-- wp:image {\"id\":484,\"sizeSlug\":\"large\",\"linkDestination\":\"none\"} -->\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large\"><img src=\"https://homemadecircus.yme.so/wp-content/uploads/2024/04/20230313-7R404981-Edit-1-e1714064953940-1024x394.jpg\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-484\"/></figure>\n<!-- /wp:image -->','FAQs','','inherit','closed','closed','','44-revision-v1','','','2024-04-25 17:11:24','2024-04-25 17:11:24','',44,'https://homemadecircus.yme.so/?p=488',0,'revision','',0),(490,3,'2024-04-25 17:12:02','2024-04-25 17:12:02','<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Click the \'+\' symbol next to any questions you\'d like the answer to. If you have any questions that are not answered below, you can email us at <a href=\"mailto:info@upswing.org.uk\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">info@upswing.org.uk</a></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:spacer {\"height\":\"11px\"} -->\n<div style=\"height:11px\" aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"wp-block-spacer\"></div>\n<!-- /wp:spacer -->\n\n<!-- wp:image {\"id\":484,\"sizeSlug\":\"large\",\"linkDestination\":\"none\"} -->\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large\"><img src=\"https://homemadecircus.yme.so/wp-content/uploads/2024/04/20230313-7R404981-Edit-1-e1714064953940-1024x394.jpg\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-484\"/></figure>\n<!-- /wp:image -->\n\n<!-- wp:spacer {\"height\":\"14px\"} -->\n<div style=\"height:14px\" aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"wp-block-spacer\"></div>\n<!-- /wp:spacer -->','FAQs','','inherit','closed','closed','','44-revision-v1','','','2024-04-25 17:12:02','2024-04-25 17:12:02','',44,'https://homemadecircus.yme.so/?p=490',0,'revision','',0),(491,3,'2024-04-25 17:12:30','2024-04-25 17:12:30','<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Click the \'+\' symbol next to any questions you\'d like the answer to. If you have any questions that are not answered below, you can email us at <a href=\"mailto:info@upswing.org.uk\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">info@upswing.org.uk</a></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:spacer {\"height\":\"11px\"} -->\n<div style=\"height:11px\" aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"wp-block-spacer\"></div>\n<!-- /wp:spacer -->\n\n<!-- wp:image {\"id\":484,\"sizeSlug\":\"large\",\"linkDestination\":\"none\"} -->\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large\"><img src=\"https://homemadecircus.yme.so/wp-content/uploads/2024/04/20230313-7R404981-Edit-1-e1714064953940-1024x394.jpg\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-484\"/></figure>\n<!-- /wp:image -->\n\n<!-- wp:spacer {\"height\":\"17px\"} -->\n<div style=\"height:17px\" aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"wp-block-spacer\"></div>\n<!-- /wp:spacer -->','FAQs','','inherit','closed','closed','','44-revision-v1','','','2024-04-25 17:12:30','2024-04-25 17:12:30','',44,'https://homemadecircus.yme.so/?p=491',0,'revision','',0),(494,3,'2024-04-25 17:30:51','2024-04-25 17:30:51','<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>The top priority when running your circus workshop is not perfecting skills, but creating a safe, judgement-free space for participants to try new things, play around, and mess up. With experimentation comes inevitable mistakes - it is key to encourage an environment where people feel comfortable being imperfect and having fun. Try putting participants at ease with these strategies:</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading -->\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Making your workshop a welcoming space</strong>:</h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:image {\"id\":456,\"sizeSlug\":\"large\",\"linkDestination\":\"none\"} -->\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large\"><img src=\"https://homemadecircus.yme.so/wp-content/uploads/2024/03/20240206-SA902108-1024x488.jpg\" alt=\"A care home staff member helps an older person to walk across the room by holding her hands\" class=\"wp-image-456\"/></figure>\n<!-- /wp:image -->\n\n<!-- wp:spacer {\"height\":\"19px\"} -->\n<div style=\"height:19px\" aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"wp-block-spacer\"></div>\n<!-- /wp:spacer -->\n\n<!-- wp:list -->\n<ul><!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><strong>Greet Everyone and Introduce Yourself -</strong> Making sure you give each participant a <strong>warm personal welcome </strong>as they enter the room, introducing yourself and being clear about what you will do together  in the session – although small, this interaction helps encourage participants to be more likely to listen and be attentive. When possible try to use people’s names when you are addressing them.</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><strong>Make eye contact</strong>&nbsp; - ensuring that you are making direct, gentle eye contact to everyone so that they understand that you are making time for them. Always use eye contact when you are working with someone on a one-to-one basis. Observe their body language and adapt the exercise if required to ensure that participants always feel comfortable</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><strong>Take your time</strong> - don’t rush the activity and go with the flow of the group. Always remember to take your time, allow for pauses so the participants can process what you\'re saying. Ensure that you demonstrate the activities clearly</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><strong>Gently get the group attention </strong>- it can get very noisy during workshops, especially when people are having a lot of fun and conversation. <strong>Try not to yell above people </strong>as this can be distressing for some. Use methods such as select gestures like waving your arms in the air and slowly one by one others will copy or stop what their doing to give your their attention. Other method include tapping / clapping a rhythm repeatedly for others to join or even singing a song</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><strong>Make it clear who’s leading and who’s supporting </strong>- there should always be one person leading the activity and others supporting. If a support-person switches to a leader role during the session - this should be clearly communicated and shown to the participants, so that they know where the instructions are coming from</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><strong>Encourage, encourage, encourage&nbsp; -</strong> At first, residents can sometimes be confused and a bit resistant to the activities. Make sure to calmly and positively reassure them, allow them to take it slow, encourage them to make mistakes and remind them that they don’t have to do it perfectly. </li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><strong>Managing other staff / helpers</strong> – As the session leader, it’s important to communicate clearly to support staff what the session plan is, how they can best support what needs to be achieved in each exercise. Your colleagues working with you in the room are your allies, use them to help you get the attention/focus of the participants so that your directions and instructions are clearly received.</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><strong>Lead with care and confidence </strong>- ensure you can be seen by everyone, try not to cover your face or mouth, speak clearly, at a steady pace and loud enough for everyone to hear. Make eye contact and repetition with a physical demonstration always helps. If you are working with seated participants you may want to consider kneeling or sitting so that you are on the same level as them</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><strong>Read the room -</strong> When working with the group, always remember to be patient and read the energy of the room. If everyone is quieter than usual play a gentle music track accompanied by a calmer activity before building up to something more energetic</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item --></ul>\n<!-- /wp:list -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading -->\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Introducing movement:</strong></h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:image {\"id\":459,\"sizeSlug\":\"large\",\"linkDestination\":\"none\"} -->\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large\"><img src=\"https://homemadecircus.yme.so/wp-content/uploads/2024/03/20240206-SA901769-1024x445.jpg\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-459\"/></figure>\n<!-- /wp:image -->\n\n<!-- wp:spacer {\"height\":\"25px\"} -->\n<div style=\"height:25px\" aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"wp-block-spacer\"></div>\n<!-- /wp:spacer -->\n\n<!-- wp:list -->\n<ul><!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>Encourage the group to follow or copy your movement - start with <strong>gentle dynamic stretches or gestures </strong>of the arms - nothing static to keep the muscles moving and encourage blood flow to warm the body up</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>Low impact dancing to music - <strong>teach the group a few movements that directly resonate to the lyrics of the music</strong> (e.g. when the song say’s up - you wave your hands up) then let them freestyle inbetween the movements or get the group to teach you some of their movements to add to the song</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>Working on <strong>dexterity</strong> - playing the piano gestures on their legs, in the air etc. opening and closing the hands and stretching the fingers to strengthen and awaken the muscles</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>Making connections - <strong>suggest to residents to greet and meet each other </strong>across the room, or next to each other by waving or sending saying hello assisted -then maybe get them to make a physical connection like a hand shake or passing an item to one another (e.g. beach ball)</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><strong>Checking in</strong> regularly with everyone to make sure that they’re comfortable, they understand what’s happening and ready to take on the next activity</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item --></ul>\n<!-- /wp:list -->','During your Workshop','','inherit','closed','closed','','314-revision-v1','','','2024-04-25 17:30:51','2024-04-25 17:30:51','',314,'https://homemadecircus.yme.so/?p=494',0,'revision','',0),(495,3,'2024-04-25 17:32:59','2024-04-25 17:32:59','Thanks for signing up to the Homemade Circus Toolkit. You should have received an email with your login details. If you can\'t see it be sure to check your spam folder just in case.','You\'re signed up!','','inherit','closed','closed','','6-revision-v1','','','2024-04-25 17:32:59','2024-04-25 17:32:59','',6,'https://homemadecircus.yme.so/?p=495',0,'revision','',0),(498,3,'2024-05-02 14:13:30','2024-05-02 14:13:30','','A Single Activity: Juggling Balls','','publish','closed','closed','','a-single-activity-juggling-balls','','','2024-06-03 16:51:07','2024-06-03 16:51:07','',0,'https://homemadecircus.yme.so/?post_type=memberpressrule&#038;p=498',0,'memberpressrule','',0),(499,3,'2024-05-02 14:24:07','2024-05-02 14:24:07','','A Single Page: Welcome to the toolkit','','publish','closed','closed','','a-single-page-welcome-to-the-toolkit','','','2024-06-03 16:50:41','2024-06-03 16:50:41','',0,'https://homemadecircus.yme.so/?post_type=memberpressrule&#038;p=499',0,'memberpressrule','',0),(500,3,'2024-05-09 12:26:30','2024-05-09 12:26:30','<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Click the \'+\' symbol next to any questions you\'d like the answer to. If you have any questions that are not answered below, you can email us at <a href=\"mailto:info@upswing.org.uk\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">info@upswing.org.uk</a></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:spacer {\"height\":\"11px\"} -->\n<div style=\"height:11px\" aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"wp-block-spacer\"></div>\n<!-- /wp:spacer -->\n\n<!-- wp:image {\"id\":484,\"sizeSlug\":\"large\",\"linkDestination\":\"none\"} -->\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large\"><img src=\"https://homemadecircus.yme.so/wp-content/uploads/2024/04/20230313-7R404981-Edit-1-e1714064953940-1024x394.jpg\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-484\"/></figure>\n<!-- /wp:image -->\n\n<!-- wp:spacer {\"height\":\"17px\"} -->\n<div style=\"height:17px\" aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"wp-block-spacer\"></div>\n<!-- /wp:spacer -->','FAQs','','inherit','closed','closed','','44-revision-v1','','','2024-05-09 12:26:30','2024-05-09 12:26:30','',44,'https://homemadecircus.yme.so/?p=500',0,'revision','',0),(501,3,'2024-05-09 12:33:21','2024-05-09 12:33:21','<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Click the \'+\' symbol next to any questions you\'d like the answer to. If you have any questions that are not answered below, you can email us at <a href=\"mailto:info@upswing.org.uk\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">info@upswing.org.uk</a></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:spacer {\"height\":\"11px\"} -->\n<div style=\"height:11px\" aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"wp-block-spacer\"></div>\n<!-- /wp:spacer -->\n\n<!-- wp:image {\"id\":484,\"sizeSlug\":\"large\",\"linkDestination\":\"none\"} -->\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large\"><img src=\"https://homemadecircus.yme.so/wp-content/uploads/2024/04/20230313-7R404981-Edit-1-e1714064953940-1024x394.jpg\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-484\"/></figure>\n<!-- /wp:image -->\n\n<!-- wp:spacer {\"height\":\"17px\"} -->\n<div style=\"height:17px\" aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"wp-block-spacer\"></div>\n<!-- /wp:spacer -->','FAQs','','inherit','closed','closed','','44-revision-v1','','','2024-05-09 12:33:21','2024-05-09 12:33:21','',44,'https://homemadecircus.yme.so/?p=501',0,'revision','',0),(504,3,'2024-05-09 12:43:07','2024-05-09 12:43:07','<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>As always, health and safety is an important consideration, especially when using new equipment. Some exercises involve touch and we always want to make sure everyone we’re working with feels completely comfortable with all parts of the activity. Follow these steps to make sure you have all the necessary Health and Safety in place before your session:</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:image {\"id\":449,\"sizeSlug\":\"large\",\"linkDestination\":\"none\"} -->\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large\"><img src=\"https://homemadecircus.yme.so/wp-content/uploads/2024/03/asd-1024x521.jpg\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-449\"/></figure>\n<!-- /wp:image -->\n\n<!-- wp:spacer {\"height\":\"24px\"} -->\n<div style=\"height:24px\" aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"wp-block-spacer\"></div>\n<!-- /wp:spacer -->\n\n<!-- wp:list -->\n<ul><!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>Make sure you <strong>fill out a risk assessment form</strong> before your workshop. You can use our template which can be found in the \'Useful Links\' section on the right-hand side of this page.<br></li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>Be sure that you have enough care home staff in the room at all times. <strong>Ideally you need 2-3 care home staff working alongside you</strong> to support you in delivering the session. Brief them on the activities, structure and Health and Safety considerations beforehand.<br></li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>Check that each participant or resident has <strong>enough space to stretch their arms and legs</strong> without clashing.<br></li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><strong>Leave space for people to exit and enter the workshop circle</strong> without disturbing the rest of the participants.<br></li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>If using touch in your session, let the person know what you are planning to do and <strong>ask permission before you touch them</strong>. For example, when using a Flower Stick to massage each others\' hands and arms, you can say \'If you want, we can try using the sticks to gently massage your arms and hands, would you be okay with that?\'.<br></li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>If you’re assisting someone in moving a part of their body you can also <strong>check with them that it feels ok and nothing is painful</strong>.<br></li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>Ensure you <strong>always do a light warm-up and cool-down</strong> before and after every session so that no one gets hurt.<br></li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item --></ul>\n<!-- /wp:list -->','Health and Safety','','inherit','closed','closed','','306-revision-v1','','','2024-05-09 12:43:07','2024-05-09 12:43:07','',306,'https://homemadecircus.yme.so/?p=504',0,'revision','',0),(506,3,'2024-05-09 12:50:06','2024-05-09 12:50:06','<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>The top priority when running your circus workshop is not perfecting skills, but creating a safe, judgement-free space for participants to try new things, play around, and mess up. With experimentation comes inevitable mistakes - it is key to encourage an environment where people feel comfortable being imperfect and having fun. Try putting participants at ease with these strategies:</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading -->\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Making your workshop a welcoming space</strong>:</h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:image {\"id\":456,\"sizeSlug\":\"large\",\"linkDestination\":\"none\"} -->\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large\"><img src=\"https://homemadecircus.yme.so/wp-content/uploads/2024/03/20240206-SA902108-1024x488.jpg\" alt=\"A care home staff member helps an older person to walk across the room by holding her hands\" class=\"wp-image-456\"/></figure>\n<!-- /wp:image -->\n\n<!-- wp:spacer {\"height\":\"19px\"} -->\n<div style=\"height:19px\" aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"wp-block-spacer\"></div>\n<!-- /wp:spacer -->\n\n<!-- wp:list -->\n<ul><!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><strong>Greet Everyone and Introduce Yourself -</strong> Making sure you give each participant a <strong>warm personal welcome </strong>as they enter the room, introducing yourself and being clear about what you will do together in the session – although small, this interaction helps encourage participants to be more likely to listen and be attentive. When possible try to use people’s names when you are addressing them</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><strong>Make eye contact</strong>&nbsp; - ensuring that you are making direct, gentle eye contact to everyone so that they understand that you are making time for them. Always use eye contact when you are working with someone on a one-to-one basis. Observe their body language and adapt the exercise if required to ensure that participants always feel comfortable</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><strong>Take your time</strong> - don’t rush the activity and go with the flow of the group. Always remember to take your time, allow for pauses so the participants can process what you\'re saying. Ensure that you demonstrate the activities clearly</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><strong>Gently get the group attention </strong>- it can get very noisy during workshops, especially when people are having a lot of fun and conversation. <strong>Try not to shout over people </strong>as this can be distressing for some. Use methods such as select gestures like waving your arms in the air and slowly one by one others will copy or stop what they\'re doing to give you their attention. Other methods include tapping / clapping a rhythm repeatedly for others to join or even singing a song</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><strong>Make it clear who’s leading and who’s supporting </strong>- there should always be one person leading the activity and others supporting. If a support-person switches to a leader role during the session - this should be clearly communicated and shown to the participants, so that they know where the instructions are coming from</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><strong>Encourage, encourage, encourage&nbsp; -</strong> At first, residents can sometimes be confused and a bit resistant to the activities. Make sure to calmly and positively reassure them, allow them to take it slow, encourage them to make mistakes and remind them that they don’t have to do it perfectly. </li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><strong>Managing other staff / helpers</strong> – As the session leader, it’s important to communicate clearly to support staff what the session plan is, how they can best support what needs to be achieved in each exercise. Your colleagues working with you in the room are your allies, use them to help you get the attention/focus of the participants so that your directions and instructions are clearly received</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><strong>Lead with care and confidence </strong>- ensure you can be seen by everyone, try not to cover your face or mouth, speak clearly, at a steady pace and loud enough for everyone to hear. Make eye contact and repetition with a physical demonstration always helps. If you are working with seated participants you may want to consider kneeling or sitting so that you are on the same level as them</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><strong>Read the room -</strong> When working with the group, always remember to be patient and read the energy of the room. If everyone is quieter than usual play a gentle music track accompanied by a calmer activity before building up to something more energetic</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item --></ul>\n<!-- /wp:list -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading -->\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Introducing movement:</strong></h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:image {\"id\":459,\"sizeSlug\":\"large\",\"linkDestination\":\"none\"} -->\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large\"><img src=\"https://homemadecircus.yme.so/wp-content/uploads/2024/03/20240206-SA901769-1024x445.jpg\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-459\"/></figure>\n<!-- /wp:image -->\n\n<!-- wp:spacer {\"height\":\"25px\"} -->\n<div style=\"height:25px\" aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"wp-block-spacer\"></div>\n<!-- /wp:spacer -->\n\n<!-- wp:list -->\n<ul><!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>Encourage the group to follow or copy your movement - start with <strong>gentle dynamic stretches or gestures </strong>of the arms - nothing static to keep the muscles moving and encourage blood flow to warm the body up</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>Low impact dancing to music - <strong>teach the group a few movements that directly resonate to the lyrics of the music</strong> (e.g. when the song says up - you wave your hands up) then let them freestyle inbetween the movements or get the group to teach you some of their movements to add to the song</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>Working on <strong>dexterity</strong> - playing the piano gestures on their legs, in the air etc. opening and closing the hands and stretching the fingers to strengthen and awaken the muscles</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>Making connections - <strong>suggest residents greet and meet each other </strong>across the room, or next to each other by waving or saying hello - then maybe get them to make a physical connection like a hand shake or passing an item to one another (e.g. beach ball)</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><strong>Checking in</strong> regularly with everyone to make sure that they’re comfortable, they understand what’s happening and are ready to take on the next activity</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item --></ul>\n<!-- /wp:list -->','During your Workshop','','inherit','closed','closed','','314-revision-v1','','','2024-05-09 12:50:06','2024-05-09 12:50:06','',314,'https://homemadecircus.yme.so/?p=506',0,'revision','',0),(508,3,'2024-05-09 12:51:53','2024-05-09 12:51:53','<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>It is nice to round-off the activities after you are finished so that everyone is left feeling content and the connected feeling continues. It is also a great time to take notes for yourself of what did and didn\'t work, so that you can focus on those in the next session. Here are some ideas of ways to close the session that will leave participants excited for the next one, choose what feels right for the room:</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading -->\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Closing the session:</strong></h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:image {\"id\":462,\"sizeSlug\":\"large\",\"linkDestination\":\"none\"} -->\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large\"><img src=\"https://homemadecircus.yme.so/wp-content/uploads/2024/03/20240206-SA901584-1024x486.jpg\" alt=\"a circus workshop leader shakes hands with an older workshop participant\" class=\"wp-image-462\"/></figure>\n<!-- /wp:image -->\n\n<!-- wp:spacer {\"height\":\"25px\"} -->\n<div style=\"height:25px\" aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"wp-block-spacer\"></div>\n<!-- /wp:spacer -->\n\n<!-- wp:list -->\n<ul><!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><strong>Cooldown</strong> and light movement/stretching</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>If the atmosphere seems lively, you can keep the music playing and <strong>use this as socialising time</strong></li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><strong>Serving tea &amp; cake</strong> whilst everyone’s together</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><strong>Remind people when the next session is</strong> while they’re in the room</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>If you’re keeping <strong>records of people’s attendance and any surprising interactions you noticed</strong>, straight after the workshop is a great time to write these down because you will be able to remember the little details more clearly, and you can also reflect on how the session went and what could be improved for next time.</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>We’d love to hear about your experience so <strong>it’s also the perfect time to send us any feedback at <a href=\"mailto:info@upswing.org.uk\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">info@upswing.org.uk</a></strong>, we would appreciate any thoughts you had about the Digital toolkit, it\'s content or how your sessions are going</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item --></ul>\n<!-- /wp:list -->','After your Workshop','','inherit','closed','closed','','317-revision-v1','','','2024-05-09 12:51:53','2024-05-09 12:51:53','',317,'https://homemadecircus.yme.so/?p=508',0,'revision','',0),(510,3,'2024-05-09 12:52:37','2024-05-09 12:52:37','<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>It is nice to round-off the activities after you are finished so that everyone is left feeling content and the connected feeling continues. It is also a great time to take notes for yourself of what did and didn\'t work, so that you can focus on those in the next session. Here are some ideas of ways to close the session that will leave participants excited for the next one, choose what feels right for the room:</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading -->\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Closing the session:</strong></h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:image {\"id\":462,\"sizeSlug\":\"large\",\"linkDestination\":\"none\"} -->\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large\"><img src=\"https://homemadecircus.yme.so/wp-content/uploads/2024/03/20240206-SA901584-1024x486.jpg\" alt=\"a circus workshop leader shakes hands with an older workshop participant\" class=\"wp-image-462\"/></figure>\n<!-- /wp:image -->\n\n<!-- wp:spacer {\"height\":\"25px\"} -->\n<div style=\"height:25px\" aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"wp-block-spacer\"></div>\n<!-- /wp:spacer -->\n\n<!-- wp:list -->\n<ul><!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><strong>Cooldown</strong> and light movement/stretching</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>If the atmosphere seems lively, you can keep the music playing and <strong>use this as socialising time</strong></li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><strong>Serving tea &amp; cake</strong> whilst everyone’s together</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><strong>Remind people when the next session is</strong> while they’re in the room</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>If you’re keeping <strong>records of people’s attendance and any surprising interactions you noticed</strong>, straight after the workshop is a great time to write these down because you will be able to remember the little details more clearly, and you can also reflect on how the session went and what could be improved for next time</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>We’d love to hear about your experience so <strong>it’s also the perfect time to send us any feedback at <a href=\"mailto:info@upswing.org.uk\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">info@upswing.org.uk</a></strong>. We would appreciate any thoughts you had about the Digital toolkit, its content or how your sessions are going</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item --></ul>\n<!-- /wp:list -->','After your Workshop','','inherit','closed','closed','','317-revision-v1','','','2024-05-09 12:52:37','2024-05-09 12:52:37','',317,'https://homemadecircus.yme.so/?p=510',0,'revision','',0),(511,3,'2024-05-09 13:33:47','2024-05-09 13:33:47','<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Click the \'+\' symbol next to any questions you\'d like the answer to. If you have any questions that are not answered below, you can email us at <a href=\"mailto:info@upswing.org.uk\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">info@upswing.org.uk</a></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:spacer {\"height\":\"11px\"} -->\n<div style=\"height:11px\" aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"wp-block-spacer\"></div>\n<!-- /wp:spacer -->\n\n<!-- wp:image {\"id\":484,\"sizeSlug\":\"large\",\"linkDestination\":\"none\"} -->\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large\"><img src=\"https://homemadecircus.yme.so/wp-content/uploads/2024/04/20230313-7R404981-Edit-1-e1714064953940-1024x394.jpg\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-484\"/></figure>\n<!-- /wp:image -->\n\n<!-- wp:spacer {\"height\":\"17px\"} -->\n<div style=\"height:17px\" aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"wp-block-spacer\"></div>\n<!-- /wp:spacer -->','FAQs','','inherit','closed','closed','','44-revision-v1','','','2024-05-09 13:33:47','2024-05-09 13:33:47','',44,'https://homemadecircus.yme.so/?p=511',0,'revision','',0),(512,3,'2024-05-09 13:34:01','2024-05-09 13:34:01','<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Click the \'+\' symbol next to any questions you\'d like the answer to. If you have any questions that are not answered below, you can email us at <a href=\"mailto:info@upswing.org.uk\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">info@upswing.org.uk</a></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:spacer {\"height\":\"11px\"} -->\n<div style=\"height:11px\" aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"wp-block-spacer\"></div>\n<!-- /wp:spacer -->\n\n<!-- wp:image {\"id\":484,\"sizeSlug\":\"large\",\"linkDestination\":\"none\"} -->\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large\"><img src=\"https://homemadecircus.yme.so/wp-content/uploads/2024/04/20230313-7R404981-Edit-1-e1714064953940-1024x394.jpg\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-484\"/></figure>\n<!-- /wp:image -->\n\n<!-- wp:spacer {\"height\":\"17px\"} -->\n<div style=\"height:17px\" aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"wp-block-spacer\"></div>\n<!-- /wp:spacer -->','FAQs','','inherit','closed','closed','','44-revision-v1','','','2024-05-09 13:34:01','2024-05-09 13:34:01','',44,'https://homemadecircus.yme.so/?p=512',0,'revision','',0),(513,3,'2024-05-09 13:34:49','2024-05-09 13:34:49','<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Click the \'+\' symbol next to any questions you\'d like the answer to. If you have any questions that are not answered below, you can email us at <a href=\"mailto:info@upswing.org.uk\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">info@upswing.org.uk</a></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:spacer {\"height\":\"11px\"} -->\n<div style=\"height:11px\" aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"wp-block-spacer\"></div>\n<!-- /wp:spacer -->\n\n<!-- wp:image {\"id\":484,\"sizeSlug\":\"large\",\"linkDestination\":\"none\"} -->\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image